hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3007","(3007) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Omar; That Abu Bakr used to teach them the tashahud on the pulpit, just as he taught the boys in the book: Greetings to God. And the prayers and good things, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. (Tahawi 264)"
"3008","(3008) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil, he said: We asked Abu Sa’id about tashahud? He said: Greetings and good prayers are for God. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. Peace be upon us and his servants. God is the righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. Abu Saeed said: We did not write anything except the Qur’an and the Tashahhud. (Abu Dawud 240)"
"3009","(3009) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Qari, who said: I witnessed Omar ibn al-Khattab teaching people the Tashahhud on the pulpit: Greetings are to God, pure things are to God, good things, prayers are to God, Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. (Malik 53)"
"3010","(3010) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, who said: I saw Aisha counting With her hand she says: The good greetings, the pure prayers are for God, peace be upon the Prophet and God’s mercy, peace be upon us and upon the servants of God. God is the righteous, I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He said: Then he prays for himself with what he appears No"
"3011","(3011) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, who said: Muhammad was asked about the Tashahhud? He said: The greetings, the good prayers, he said: Then he said: Ibn Abbas used to increase in them, the blessings."
"3012","(3012) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim; Alqamah used to teach Bedouins the Tashhud, and Alqamah would say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and may God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. And I forgave him, so the Bedouins celebrated the feast, and Alqamah said: This is what we taught."
"3013","(3013) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: He heard Ibrahim teaching the tashahud, greetings to God and good things. And the prayers, peace be upon you, O Prophet, and God’s mercy and blessings, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God, I bear witness that There is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"3014","(3014) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He did not say in the two rak'ahs: Peace be upon you, O Prophet. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God."
"3015","(3015) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have been given the beginnings of the speech, its conclusions, and its conclusions. He said: So we said: We learned from what May God teach you, he said: So he taught us the Tashahhud."
"3016","(3016) Hushaym told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he teaches us the tashahud in prayer, just as the scribe teaches the children. (Abu Ali 5605)"
"3017","(3017) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Salami, who said: We were We learn the Tashahhud just as we learn the surahs from the Qur’an."
"3018","(3018) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I saw Alqamah learning the Tash-hud from Abdullah Just as he learns surahs from the Qur’an."
"3019","(3019) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid told us, he said: Abu al-Zubair told me, on the authority of Tawoos, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud, just as he taught us the surahs from the Qur’an. (Muslim 3031, Ahmad 1/315)"
"3020","(3020) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to memorize this tashudah. Abdullah, and they follow its letters, letter by letter."
"3021","(3021) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jami’ bin Abi Rashid, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach us the Tashahhud just as he taught us the surahs from the Qur’an. (Abu Dawud 961. Ahmed 394)q"
"3022","(3022) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id al-Nakha’i, who said: I came to Ibn Masoud with my father, so he taught us This tashahhud means the tashahhud of Abdullah."
"3023","(3023) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: We were not writing about From the hadiths of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for the Istikharah and the Tashahhud."
"3024","(3024) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah used to teach us the tashahud in Prayer, just as the surahs from the Qur’an teach us, taking upon us the alif and waw."
"3025","(3025) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: Ibn Abbas heard a man He was praying, and when he sat reciting the tashahhud, he said: Praise be to God. Greetings are to God. He said: Ibn Abbas said: And he was concluding. Praise be to God. When you sit, start reciting the Tashahid, with: Greetings to God."
"3026","(3026) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to take the waw in the tash-hud from us. Prayers and good things."
"3027","(3027) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were learning the Tash-hud, just as they are learning Surahs from the Qur’an."
"3028","(3028) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ayman, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the tashahhud: In the name of God."
"3029","(3029) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Omar said in the tashhud: In the name of God."
"3030","(3030) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; When he recited the tashahhud, he used to say: In the name of God. The best of the names is the name of God."
"3031","(3031) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, who said: Ibn Masoud heard a man saying in Tashkud: In the name of God. He said: This is only said about food."
"3032","(3032) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to say in the tashahhud: In the name of God."
"3033","(3033) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abi Ubaidah, on the authority of his father Abdullah bin Masoud: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sat in the first two rak’ahs, it was as if he was on his knees. I said: Until he gets up? He said: Until he rises. (Abu Dawud 987. Ahmad 1/386)"
"3034","(3034) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, who said: Whenever Abu Bakr sat in the two rak’ahs As if he was on his knees, meaning until he stood up."
"3035","(3035) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of a man who prayed behind Abu Bakr; In the first two rak'ahs, it was as if he were on hot coals until he got up."
"3036","(3036) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to sit in the tashahhud in the two rak'ahs for as long as the tashahhud was recited, then stand up."
"3037","(3037) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Iyad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: The palm of the hand is not placed in the two rak’ahs except for the Tashahhud."
"3038","(3038) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: The first two rak’ahs do not exceed the tash-hud."
"3039","(3039) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Na’im al-Qari, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: Whoever prays more in the first two rak’ahs On the tashahhud, he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"3040","(3040) Abd al-Salam told us, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu al-Jawzai, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the two rak’ahs: Greetings. (Abu Dawud 772)"
"3041","(3041) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, who said: I heard Mus’ab bin Saad narrating on the authority of Saad; When he recited the tashahhud, he would say: Glory be to God, He filled the heavens and filled the earth, and what is between them, and what is under the earth, and praise be to God, He filled The heavens and the filling of the earth, and what is between them, and what is under the earth. And God is Great. The filling of the heavens and the filling of the earth, and what is between them, and what is under them. Under the dust, his people said: I do not know which God is greater before, or praise be to God, and praise be to God, good and blessed praise, There is no god but God alone, with no partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. Oh God, I am I ask you of all good things, then he greets you."
"3042","(3042) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, who said: Abdullah used to teach us the tashahud in prayer, then he says: If one of you has finished reciting the Tashahhud during the prayer, let him say: O God, I ask you of all goodness. I knew of it and what I did not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I knew of it and what I did not know. Oh God, I ask you of goodness. Whatever Your righteous servants ask of You, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of which Your righteous servants seek refuge from. Our Lord, give us in this world what is good and fulfill it. The Hereafter is good, and protect us from the torment of the Fire. Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us our sins, and atone for us our evil deeds, and we will die with the righteous. Our Lord, and give us what you promised us among your messengers[corrupt] And do not disgrace us on the Day of Resurrection, for you will not break your promise."
"3043","(3043) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, and Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The man recites the Tashahid, then sends blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then says supplication for himself."
"3044","(3044) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When you have finished reciting the Tashahhud, then pray for your hereafter. And your world is what it seemed to you."
"3045","(3045) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that they both said: Pray in your prayer. Whatever you want"
"3046","(3046) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: I said to Mujahid: I pray for myself in What is written? He said: Do not pray for yourself until you witness the tashahhud. He said: I asked Ata’, and he said: Be careful about asking for forgiveness."
"3047","(3047) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to like to invite the imam after Reciting five comprehensive words: O God, we ask you of all goodness, what we know of it, and what we do not know, and we seek refuge in You. Of all evil, what we know of it, and what we do not know. He said: Whatever the Imam hastens with, let him not hasten with these words."
"3048","(3048) Hammad bin Masadhi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Aoun, who said: Abdullah said: Pray in your prayers. With your most important needs to you."
"3049","(3049) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Aoun, who said: Make your needs fulfilled in prayer. The virtue of supplication in it is the same as the virtue of the voluntary prayer."
"3050","(3050) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: Whenever Abu Musa had finished His prayer, he said: O God, forgive me my sins, make my affairs easy for me, and bless my livelihood for me."
"3051","(3051) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to prefer to supplicate in the written supplications with supplications. The Qur’an."
"3052","(3052) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sadiqa ibn Yasar, who said: I heard Tawus saying: Pray in the obligatory prayer according to what In the Qur’an."
"3053","(3053) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, similar to the hadith of Tawoos."
"3054","(3054) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sadiqah bin Yasar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Pray in the obligatory prayers including The Qur’an, or he said: in the Written."
"3055","(3055) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: I heard Muhammad, and he was asked about supplications in prayer? He said: The most beloved of their supplications was that which agreed with the Qur’an."
"3056","(3056) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He was disliked to supplicate during prayer. With some matter of this world."
"3057","(3057) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; It was astonishing for him to pray in the written, including what is in the Qur’an."
"3058","(3058) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Thabit, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad. On the authority of Amer bin Saad, on the authority of Saad, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to greet him on his right, and on the Left, until the whites of her cheeks can be seen. (Muslim 1198, Ahmad 1/173)"
"3059","(3059) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Al-Bakhtari narrating, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Al-Yahsbi, on the authority of Wael Al-Hadrami; He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he used to say “Allahu Akbar” when he lowered and when he raised it, and he raised his hands when Takbeer, and he says salaam to his right and to his left.\n Shu`ba said: Aban bin Taghlib said to me: In the hadith: until his face appears clear, so I said to Amr: In the hadith : Until his face appears clear, and he said: Or something like that. (Ahmad 4/316, Tayalisi 1021)"
"3060","(3060) Omar bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s peace and blessings be upon you. He greets you from his right until the whites of his cheeks are visible: May God’s peace and mercy be upon you, and may God’s mercy and blessings be upon you. Like that (Ahmad 1/448, Abu Dawud 988)"
"3061","(3061) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salutation during prayer on his right and on his left until white could be seen. His face and says: May God’s peace and mercy be upon you, from both sides."
"3062","(3062) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to greet him to his right and to his left: May peace and God’s mercy be upon you, until He sees the white of her cheek. (Tahawi 269. Darqutni 357)"
"3063","(3063) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to greet him on the right and on the Sarah, Abu Bakr, and Omar. (Nasa’i 1242 and Tayalisi 279)"
"3064","(3064) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Salih, on the authority of Salma ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Hujr ibn Anbas, on the authority of Wa’il Bin Hajar; He prayed behind the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and when he read the book, he uttered an “Amen” and said: “And he greeted us on his right.” And to his left, until I saw the whites of his cheeks."
"3065","(3065) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, he said: He mentioned the salutation in the presence of a brother, and he said: I prayed behind Omar. And Abdullah, both of them greeted him, saying: Peace be upon you and God’s mercy. Peace be upon you and God’s mercy."
"3066","(3066) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Harithah bin Mudarib, who said: I prayed behind Ammar, so he said the salaam on the authority of To his right and to his left: May God’s peace and mercy be upon you."
"3067","(3067) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It is as if I am looking at the white of the cheek of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted when he greeted: May God’s peace and mercy be upon you, peace. May God have mercy on you. (Ahmed 465)"
"3068","(3068) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq ibn Salamah, who said: I prayed behind Ali, so he said the salaam on his right. And to his left: Peace be upon you and God’s mercy. Peace be upon you and God’s mercy."
"3069","(3069) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, who said: I heard Abu Razin saying: I heard Ali greeting Praying from the right and from the left, and the one from the left is shorter."
"3070","(3070) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Suwayd, he said: Alqamah was He saluted from his right: Peace be upon you and God’s mercy, and from his left: Peace be upon you and God’s mercy. He said: And it was Black says on his right: Peace, God’s mercy, and blessings be upon you, and on his left: May God’s peace, mercy, and blessings be upon you. And His blessings."
"3071","(3071) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Khaythami, that he said: Peace be upon you. May God have mercy on him, may God’s peace and mercy be upon you."
"3072","(3072) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to greet us during prayer, saying: Peace be upon you. May God have mercy on him, may God’s peace and mercy be upon you."
"3073","(3073) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman; He used to greet him from his right: peace be upon you and God’s mercy, and from his left: peace be upon you and God’s mercy."
"3074","(3074) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to say salutations from his right: “Peace be upon you and God’s mercy” and raising his voice therewith, and from his left: “Peace be upon you.” May God have mercy on you, lower than the first."
"3075","(3075) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Saeed and Ammar greeted each other with two salutations."
"3076","(3076) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father; The imam of Masruq’s mosque was giving two salaams, so we said to Masruq? He said: I ordered him to do that."
"3077","(3077) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla; He used to say salutations to his right and to his left: Peace be upon you, peace be upon you."
"3078","(3078) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah; It was said to him: A man from the people of Mecca is offering two greetings, so Abdullah said: Did he hang it? ! (Muslim 117)"
"3079","(3079) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Yazid, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun; He used to offer two salutations."
"3080","(3080) Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He used to offer two salutations."
"3081","(3081) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar used to greet each other with one salutation. (Ibn Majah 920, Bayhaqi 179)"
"3082","(3082) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Anas used to greet one person."
"3083","(3083) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Marzban, who said: I prayed behind Ibn Abi Layla, so he said one salutation, then I prayed behind Ali and he said one salutation."
"3084","(3084) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan; That Abu Wael used to greet him with greetings."
"3085","(3085) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab; He used to offer his salutations."
"3086","(3086) Saal bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz, so he said one salutation."
"3087","(3087) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They were both submitting to their faith, and I prayed behind Al-Qasim, but I do not know of him who differed from them."
"3088","(3088) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to offer his salutations."
"3089","(3089) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Jabir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, greeted him with salutations."
"3090","(3090) Abu Bakr told us, he informed me on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; She used to greet him with peace. (Ibn Khuzaymah 732, Bayhaqi 179)"
"3091","(3091) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Dirham, who said: I saw Anas, Al-Hasan, Aba Al-Aliyah, and Aba Raja’. They greet you with peace."
"3092","(3092) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Zaid, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Awfa greeting him with salutations."
"3093","(3093) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to offer his salutations."
"3094","(3094) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Waqa’i; Saeed bin Jubayr used to greet him with salutations."
"3095","(3095) Musaab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd; He used to give one salutation."
"3096","(3096) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, that he used to greet him with salutations."
"3097","(3097) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: When Abdullah finished the prayer, he would turn his back. quickly, so he will either stand up, or he will deviate."
"3098","(3098) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, and Khalid, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When the Imam said the salaam, He got up, and Khaled said: He deviated."
"3099","(3099) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: I prayed behind Ali, so he said the salaam on his right and on the right. He walked away, then jumped as he had done."
"3100","(3100) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar said: The imam’s sitting after the salutation is an innovation."
"3101","(3101) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah used to greet It is as if he is on his knees, until he gets up."
"3102","(3102) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. When he greets, he does not sit except as long as he says: O God, you are the peace and from you is peace. Blessed are you, Lord of Majesty. And honor. (Muslim 1368, Tirmidhi 299)"
"3103","(3103) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Awsaja ibn al-Rammah, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Dhudhail, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say the salutation, he would not sit except as much as he would say, O God, you are the peace, and to you be peace. Peace, Blessed be You, O Possessor of Glory and Honor. (Ibn Hibban 2002 and Ibn Khuzaymah 736)"
"3104","(3104) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: We had an imam, who mentioned His grace, when he greets, he advances."
"3105","(3105) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Every prayer after which there is a voluntary prayer and a change in prayer, except for the afternoon prayer. And dawn."
"3106","(3106) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: As for Morocco, do not let it go."
"3107","(3107) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’, on the authority of al-Hasan, that when he said the salaam, he would turn aside or stand up quickly."
"3108","(3108) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, that when he said the salaam, he would stand up and go as he was. And he did not sit."
"3109","(3109) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that when he greeted, he would turn away and face the people."
"3110","(3110) Hushaym told us, saying: Ali bin Ata told us, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid bin Al-Aswad Al-Amiri, on the authority of His father, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at dawn, and when he said the salaam, he departed. (Tirmidhi 219. Ahmad 161)"
"3111","(3111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab; When Ali left, he faced the people facing him."
"3112","(3112) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, he said: A sheikh narrated to me, on the authority of Salah bin He exhaled and said: I heard Ibn Umar saying at the end of the prayer: O God, You are peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are you, Possessor of majesty and honor."
"3113","(3113) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Ward, the client of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bi, he said : Muawiyah wrote to Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba: What the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say, when he greeted someone Prayer? He said: So he dictated it to Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, and he wrote it to Muawiyah, saying that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace When he said the salutation, he used to say: There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He is capable of all things. Oh God, there is no one who can prevent what You have given, nor can there be a giver of what You have withheld, and no one can benefit from your earnestness from you. \n(Muslim 415. Abu Dawud 1500)"
"3114","(3114) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted us more than once, saying at the end of his prayer when he finished: Glory be to your Lord, Lord of glory, above what they describe, and peace be upon the messengers. Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds. (Taalisi 2198, Abu Ali 1118)"
"3115","(3115) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Husayn bin Yazid Al-Thaalabi, On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud; When he finished praying, he used to say: Oh God, I ask you among the causes of your mercy and the confirmation of your forgiveness, and I ask you The spoils are from all righteousness, and safety from all sin. Oh God, I ask you to win Paradise and escape from Hell. Oh God, no Leave no sin for us except that You forgive it, no worry except that You relieve it, and no need except that You fulfill it."
"3116","(3116) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Salam ibn Shaddad al-Jariri, on the authority of Ghazwan ibn Jarir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali When he said the salaam, he said: There is no god but Allah, and we worship none but Allah."
"3117","(3117) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Awsaja, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Dhudhayl, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Asim On the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he said hello: Oh God, you are the peace and from you is peace. However, in the hadith of Abdullah: And to you is peace. Blessed are you, O possessor of majesty and honor."
"3118","(3118) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: When Abraham greeted us, he would turn to us with his face and say: No. There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner."
"3119","(3119) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Ubaidah and I passed by in The mosque, and Musaab was leading the people in prayer. When he left, he said: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest. He raised his voice with it and said: `Ubaidah: May God Almighty kill him, he will scold him for heresies."
"3120","(3120) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Dhayl, he said: They used to say, “When they departed from Prayer: O God, You are peace and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor."
"3121","(3121) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I mentioned to Al-Qasim that a man from the people of Yemen mentioned to me: When the imam said the salaam from the obligatory prayer, the people used to say “Allahu Akbar” three times, or “Talahilaat.” Then the Qasim said: “By God! Ibn al-Zubayr would have done that."
"3122","(3122) Muhammad ibn Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Abraham was asked about the imam, if he saluted, he would say: May the peace of God be upon Muhammad, and no. There is no god but Allah? He said: No one before them had done this."
"3123","(3123) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: This Heresy"
"3124","(3124) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih informed me, he said: Malik ibn Ziyad al-Ashja’i narrated to me. He said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz saying: Part of the completion of the prayer is to say when you have finished: There is no god but Allah, alone, with whom there is no partner. To Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things, three times."
"3125","(3125) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: Abdullah said: They will not make us One of you gives Satan a part of himself, and he only sees that it is his right not to turn away except from his right hand, more I never saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, turn away from his left side. (Bukhari 852, Abu Dawud 1035)"
"3126","(3126) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Qubaysah ibn Halab speaking, on the authority of His father; He prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw him turn away from his wretchedness. (Ahmad 2271, Tayalisi 1087)"
"3127","(3127) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to turn away from his right hand. (Muslim 61. Ahmad 280)"
"3128","(3128) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you finish the prayer and you want A pilgrim, and whether your need is on your right or on your left, then take the direction of your need."
"3129","(3129) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Salam ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Ghazwan ibn Jarir, on the authority of his father; When Ali greeted, he did not care whether he turned to his right or to his left."
"3130","(3130) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He hated for a man to turn around during his prayer, just as a donkey turns around during his prayer."
"3131","(3131) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya; Abu Ubaidah saw a man who left his path and said: This man has followed the Sunnah."
"3132","(3132) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to prefer that a man turn away from his prayer to his right."
"3133","(3133) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi’ ibn Hibban said: I was praying, and Ibn Umar was leaning his back against the wall of the qibla, so I turned away from my walk, and he said: What prevents you from turning to your right? I said: No, except that I saw you and turned to you, and he said: You are correct. People say: Turn to your right, so if You were praying, so leave, if you like, to your right or to your left."
"3134","(3134) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Leave as you wish."
"3135","(3135) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Walid Al-Bajli, he said: Abdullah said: On you. With the limit of prayer; The first takbeerah."
"3136","(3136) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, who said: The early morning prayer is the takbirah. The first"
"3137","(3137) Abu Usama narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa Yazid bin Sinan, he said: Abu Ubaid Al-Hajib narrated to us, he said: I heard An old man in the Sacred Mosque said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Indeed, everything has a nose. And if he completed the first takbirah prayer, then observe it. Abu Ubaid said: I narrated it to Raja’ ibn Hawwah, and he said: Umm al-Darda’ narrated to me, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’. (Musnad 46)"
"3138","(3138) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Al-Rayyan Al-Rasib, on the authority of the sheikhs of Banu Rasib; Talha and Al-Zubayr prayed in one of their mosques, but the imam was not there. Then, we said to them: Let one of you come forward. You are both companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. But they refused and said: Where is the Imam? Where is the Imam? Then the imam came and led them in prayer. They said: All your prayers were close, except for something I saw you doing, and it was not good in it. Your prayers, so we said: What is it? They said: When the Imam greets, no man should stand up from behind him until the Imam turns to face him, or gets up from his place."
"3139","(3139) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim that they said: He does not make up until The imam deviates."
"3140","(3140) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour and Khaled told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, he said: I said to Ibn Omar: I come first. Part of the prayer, and the imam says salaam, so I stand up and perform what I did earlier, or do I wait for him to deviate? Ibn Omar said: When the Imam said the salutation, he would stand up, and Khalid said: When the Imam said the salutation, he would recline, and reclining was with the salutation."
"3141","(3141) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; Concerning a man who performed one or two rak’ahs before me? He said: He does not stand up if the imam says the salaam until he turns away or stands up."
"3142","(3142) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about the imam if he said the salaam and then did not deviate? He said: Leave him until he finishes his heresy, but he hated for him to get up and make up for it."
"3143","(3143) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: When he greets The Imam says, “Get up and do whatever you want.” He says: Do not wait for him to rise, and do not turn away from his seat."
"3144","(3144) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to judge, and did not wait for the imam. He said: And the Qasim, the Salem, and the Helper used to do that."
"3145","(3145) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Harun told us, he said: I prayed in Medina and I was ahead of it in some of the prayers, so when he gave the salutation Imam: I got up to fulfill what I had done earlier, but a man who was next to me pulled me away and said: You should not have gotten up. Until he deviates, he said: I met Abu Sa`id and mentioned that to him, and it was as if he did not dislike what I did, or what I said to him. Like it"
"3146","(3146) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: O my son, When I say the salutation, I sit and say “Allahu Akbar” and “Allahu Akbar.” Whoever has any prayer left to do, let him stand up and make up for it."
"3147","(3147) Ruh bin Ubadah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will wait for him for a little while, then if he sits, get up and leave him."
"3148","(3148) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to return greetings to the Imam."
"3149","(3149) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the imam greets him and he responds to him."
"3150","(3150) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Salim, who said: If the imam greets him and he responds to him."
"3151","(3151) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, who said: I said to Abraham: When Dhar greets the imam, he responds to him. He said: It is sufficient for him to salute on his right and on his left."
"3152","(3152) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: When the imam greets, let those behind him respond to him."
"3153","(3153) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Abu Aqeel narrated to me; He saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab saluting to his right and to his left, then responding to the imam."
"3154","(3154) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of his father, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Omar. He saw a man whose face was affected by prostration, and he said: The man’s appearance is his face, so let none of you disgrace his appearance."
"3155","(3155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu Awn al-A’war, on the authority of Abu al-Darda’; He saw a woman with something like the backs of a sheep, so he said: This is what if it had not been between your eyes. It was better for you."
"3156","(3156) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, who said: I said to Maymunah: Have you not seen? Someone taps his forehead on the ground, wanting to touch it with the effect of prostration. She said: Leave him so that he may enter."
"3157","(3157) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He hated the effect on the face."
"3158","(3158) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Musafir Al-Jassas, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: I complained to Mujahid. The mark was between my eyes, and he said to me: When you prostrate, then dry yourself."
"3159","(3159) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw the companions of Ali and the companions of Abdullah And traces of prostration were on their foreheads and noses."
"3160","(3160) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I have never seen a greater prostration than her, meaning he prostrated. Ibn Al-Zubayr."
"3161","(3161) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I saw the people of the people of Banu Abd Qais dominating the land. Like a camel's carcass."
"3162","(3162) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Hasan, they said: When the mosque was built, they said: O Messenger of God, How do we build it? He said: A throne like the throne of Moses."
"3163","(3163) Ibn Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: A man narrated to me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: It was said: A time will come upon the people when they will build mosques and boast about them, but they will not inhabit them except for a little while. (Abu Dawud 450. An-Nasa’i 768)"
"3164","(3164) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Asam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: I have not been commanded to build mosques. (Abdul Razzaq 5127)"
"3165","(3165) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: That you may adorn it as the Jews and Christians have adorned it."
"3166","(3166) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed, he said: My father said: If You have beautified your mosques and beautified your Qur’an, then destruction will be upon you."
"3167","(3167) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Muslim al-Batin, who said: He passed by a mosque that had been honoured, He said: This was sold to the son of so-and-so."
"3168","(3168) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, who said: Abdullah bin Shaqiq said: The mosques were numerous, but they were The honor of people is a matter of eternity."
"3169","(3169) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Musa, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: We were commanded to build all mosques. And the cities are honorable."
"3170","(3170) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Let your mosques be decorated. Just as the Jews and Christians decorated their mosques."
"3171","(3171) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Build mosques and take them as a whole."
"3172","(3172) Malik narrated to us, he said: Hareem narrated to us, he said: Laith narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were forbidden, Or he forbade us from praying in an honorable mosque. (Tabarani 13499, Bayhaqi 439)"
"3173","(3173) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: Who built A mosque for God, even if it were like a patch of sand. A house was built for him in Paradise."
"3174","(3174) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Yazid bin Abdul Aziz told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: Whoever builds a mosque for God, even if he has checked its tiles, God built a house for him in Paradise. (Ibn Hibban 1611. Tabarani 1105)"
"3175","(3175) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Asama, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Al-Walid, on the authority of Othman bin Abdullah bin Suraqi, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, that he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: Whoever builds a mosque in which the name of God is mentioned, God will build a house for him in Paradise. \n(Ibn Majah 2758 and Ibn Hibban 1608)"
"3176","(3176) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Whoever builds a mosque with its floors clean, God will build for him a house in Paradise.\n(Ahmad 241. Tayalisi 2617)"
"3177","(3177) Abu Bakr said: I found in my father’s book: on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid On the authority of Uthman, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: Whoever builds a mosque, even if he examines its floors, God will build for him a house in Heaven"
"3178","(3178) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ata`, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever builds a mosque, God will build a house for him. It was said: And these are the mosques on the way to Mecca? She said: And these are the mosques on the way to Mecca."
"3179","(3179) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He came A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: One of us prays in one garment, so he said: Do you all have two garments? Abu Hurairah said to the one who asked him: Do you know Abu Hurairah? He prays in a garment. (Ibn Hibban 2296 and Ahmad 2/239)"
"3180","(3180) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in one garment, wrapped in it. (Muslim 2851, Ahmad 3/10)"
"3181","(3181) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in one garment, protecting himself from the heat and cold of the earth."
"3182","(3182) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked May the peace and blessings of God be upon him about praying in a garment? He said: Do you all have two dresses? (Bukhari 3651, Muslim 368)"
"3183","(3183) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If your garment is spacious, then wrap yourself in it, and if it is narrow, then wrap yourselves around it. (Ibn Saad 30)"
"3184","(3184) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qays bin Talq bin Ali, on the authority of his father, he said: He came A man said: O Prophet of God, what do you think of praying in one garment? He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, loosened his garment and tore it off with his robe, then he covered himself with it and then led us in prayer. When He finished the prayer and said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"3185","(3185) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in one garment."
"3186","(3186) Abdullah bin Ajlah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in a garment. One disagreed between the two parties. (Nasa’i 860. Ahmad 3/243)"
"3187","(3187) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, who said: Khaled bin Al-Walid used to go out He leads the people in prayer in one garment."
"3188","(3188) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: Ibn Abbas was asked about a man who prays in"
"3189","(3189) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A man came to Aisha and said: I should pray in a garment. One? She said: Yes, and there is a difference between the two sides."
"3190","(3190) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Qays ibn Abi Hazim, who said: Khaled ibn al-Walid led us in prayer. In one garment in the delegations, with its two ends separated, and behind it were the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3191","(3191) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Anas was asked about praying in a garment? He said: He should cover himself with it."
"3192","(3192) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hallam, on the authority of Masoud, meaning Ibn Harash, who said: Omar led us in prayer in a garment that was not worn. Others, he said: And Masoud, meaning Ibn Harash, believed us in Batt."
"3193",""
"3194","(3194) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to pray in a garment."
"3195","(3195) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdullah bin Hunayn, on the authority of Abu The client of Aqeel bin Abi Talib passed by, on the authority of Umm Hani’ Ibn Abi Talib, who said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and water was poured for him, so he bathed, then he gathered his clothes and crossed his two ends on his shoulders, then he prayed the forenoon prayer, eight times. Rakat"
"3196","(3196) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhri, who said: My father said: Praying in one garment is good. We did it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"3197","(3197) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: I asked him about praying in one’s garment, or Was he asked? He said: It differs between its two extremes."
"3198","(3198) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: I asked Abu Salama bin Abd al-Rahman about Praying in one garment? He said: I pray in one garment, and next to me are other clothes. If I wanted to take some of it, I would take it."
"3199","(3199) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Mughiriya, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah; Ali said: There is no harm in praying in one garment, or praying in one garment."
"3200","(3200) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man praying in one garment, he said: It is good, as long as his two ends are separated."
"3201","(3201) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, prays in one garment, wrapping himself in it. (Muslim 283"
"3202","(3202) Waki’ told us, he said: Aban bin Sam’a told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in prayer. In one garment."
"3203","(3203) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; He used to say: He prays in one garment, some of which he wraps around, and some of which he wears."
"3204","(3204) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Salama bin Al-Akwa’, who said: Salama used to pray in A dress"
"3205","(3205) Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Yunus narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Al-Harith Al-Muharbi narrated to us, saying: I heard Ghaylan bin Comprehensive, he said: Iyas bin Salamah told me, on the authority of Ibn Ammar bin Yasser, he said: My father said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, believed in us. He greeted me in one garment, wearing it. (Abu Yali 1635)"
"3206","(3206) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Amr bin Kathir told us, he said: Ibn Kaysan told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying the noon and afternoon prayers in one garment, wearing it. (Ibn Majah 1051. Ahmad 3/417)"
"3207","(3207) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Abu Nadhru, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b and Ibn Masoud disagreed about praying in one garment, so Ubayy said: a garment, and he said: Ibn Masoud: Thawban, then Omar came out to them and blamed them, and said: It would be unpleasant for two of Muhammad’s companions to disagree. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him regarding the one thing, so which of your two young men will people turn to? As for Ibn Masoud, he did not say anything, and the statement is what Ubayy said. (Bayhaqi 238)"
"3208","(3208) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He prays in a garment. The one wearing it, and Ibn Omar said: It will not harm him if he has antiques until he takes out one of his hands."
"3209","(3209) Yahya bin Ishaq told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, he said: Yahya the Umayyad told us, He said: I and Ezra bin Abi Qais entered upon Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Juzi’ al-Zubaidi, and she was his companion. So he performed ablution and prayed in one garment, with its two ends separated."
"3210","(3210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he prays in the house of Umm Salamah in a garment, placing the ends of it on his shoulders. (Tirmidhi 339, Abu Dawud 628)"
"3211","(3211) Waki’ told us, he said: Fudail bin Ghazwan told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I saw Seventy of the People of the Saffah pray in one garment, some of them reach the knees, and some of them are below Therefore, when he bows, he holds himself tight for fear that his private parts will be exposed."
"3212","(3212) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Mughiryah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah said: Ali said: If a man prays in one garment, then he should cover himself with it."
"3213","(3213) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Jabir bin Abdullah came to us in one garment, fully clothed. With it"
"3214","(3214) Muhammad bin Omar Al-Aslami told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Uthman told us, on the authority of Habib, Urwa’s servant, he said: I heard Asma’ bint Abi Bakr said: I saw my father praying in one garment, so I said: O father, should you pray in one garment? And your clothes are on? He said: O my sons, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the last prayer behind me in one garment. (Abu Ali 51)"
"3215","(3215) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a man praying covered, so he said: Do not imitate the Jews, those of you who do not find anything except a garment. One, let him girdle himself with it."
"3216","(3216) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I saw him praying in a garment wearing a wrap. With it"
"3217","(3217) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Ata, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Naam say: : Abu Saeed was asked about praying in one garment? He said: He girdles himself with it just as he girdles himself for war."
"3218","(3218) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I heard Hayyan al-Bariqi, he said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: If I had only found One garment that I used to wrap myself in is more beloved to me than to wrap myself around myself in it as the Jews would cover themselves with it."
"3219","(3219) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If a man wants to pray and he has nothing but a garment. One who girds himself with Him."
"3220","(3220) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, who said: Abdullah bin Abi Mulki led us in prayer in one garment. He raised him to his chest."
"3221","(3221) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Nafi’ ibn Umar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed with a cripple in one garment, which he raised to his chest."
"3222","(3222) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Waqid, who said: I prayed next to Abdullah ibn Omar, while I was fully clothed, ordered me to wear a loincloth."
"3223","(3223) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not pray in one garment. Unless you find nothing else."
"3224","(3224) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Suleiman bin Qurum narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Abu Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: Do not pray in a garment, even if it is as wide as between the heavens and the earth."
"3225","(3225) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I saw Abu Qalabab wearing a robe and a washed quilt, and he"
"3226","(3226) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: It was said to Al-Hasan: They say that it is disliked for a man to pray. And he took his hand out from under his throat, and Al-Hasan said: If God had entrusted His religion to these people, they would have imposed hardship on His servants."
"3227","(3227) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan ibn Umair, who said: I was with Qais ibn Abbad, and he saw A man was praying, and he took his hand out from his neck and said: Go to your friend and tell him: Let him put his hand down from a place. The hand of the fettered person, so I came to him and said to him: A Qais says: Put your hand down from where the hand of the fettered man was. He said: So he put it down."
"3228","(3228) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I saw him praying, holding his robe beneath his upper arm."
"3229","(3229) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Eizar, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, which work is best? He said: Prayer for its time. (Bukhari 527. Tirmidhi 1898)"
"3230","(3230) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; {Those who are constant in their prayers} He said: On its appointed times."
"3231","(3231) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I was informed that Abu Bakr and Omar used to teach the people: to worship. God, and do not associate anything with Him, and perform the prayer that God has provided for its times, for if you neglect it, you will perish."
"3232","(3232) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Preserving the prayer, the prayer. Immediately"
"3233","(3233) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, he said: Al-Aswad was only a monk, and he lagged behind. He prays, so when the time for prayer comes, he prostrates himself, even on stones."
"3234","(3234) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to us: As for what follows, The essence of the religion and the foundation of Islam is faith in God, establishing prayer, and paying zakat. Perform the prayer at its appointed time, and memorize it. Aliyah"
"3235","(3235) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; It was a wonder for him, when he was travelling, to perform the prayer at its proper time."
"3236","(3236) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Omar ibn Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I said to him: Which prayer is best? He said: At the first time."
"3237","(3237) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Mus`ab ibn Sa`d, on the authority of Sa`d, he said: The forgetfulness: Abandoning time."
"3238","(3238) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Umari narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ghanam, on the authority of some of his mothers, on the authority of Umm Farwa; She asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Which work, or which prayer, is better? He said: Prayer at the beginning of its time."
"3239","(3239) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Ayyash bin Abi Rabi’ah, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim bin Abbad bin Hanif, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Gabriel made me stop at the House twice, and he led me in the noon prayer when the sun had passed and it was as high as Shirak, and he led the afternoon prayer with me when everything was in the same shade, and he led the sunset prayer with me when the fasting person broke his fast, and he led the prayer with me He performed the evening prayer when twilight had disappeared, he performed the dawn prayer with me when food and drink were forbidden to the fasting person, and he performed the noon prayer with me tomorrow when there was complete shade. Something like it, and he led the afternoon prayer with me when the shade of everything was like it, and he led the sunset prayer with me when the fasting person broke his fast, He led me in the evening prayer for a third of the night, and he led me in the dawn prayer when he left, then he turned to me and said: O Muhammad, this time is the time The prophets before you, the time is between these two times.\n(Tirmidhi 149 Abu Dawud 396)"
"3240","(3240) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Badr bin Othman, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, who heard it from him, on the authority of his father; That a questioner came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and asked him about the times for prayer, but he did not answer anything. He said: Then he ordered Bilal So he stood until dawn broke and prayed, then he ordered him to perform the prayer. Someone said: The sun has set, or has not set, and it was. He was more knowledgeable than them. Then he ordered him to perform the afternoon prayer while the sun was high. He ordered him to perform the sunset prayer when the sun had set. He ordered him to perform the sunset prayer when the sun had set. He ordered him to perform the sunset prayer when the sun had set. Isha’ prayer when twilight falls, then he prays Fajr the next day. The one who said it says: The sun has risen, or it has not risen, and He knows best. Among them, he prayed the noon prayer, close to the time of the afternoon prayer yesterday, and he prayed the afternoon prayer, and the one who says: The sun has turned red, and he prayed the sunset prayer. Before twilight set, he prayed Isha' for the first third of the night, then he said: Where is the one who asked about the time? There is time between these two times. (Muslim 178. Abu Dawud 398)"
"3241","(3241) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: There is a beginning and an end to prayer, and the beginning of the time for noon is when the sun has set, and the end of its time is when the time for The beginning of the time for the afternoon is when the time for the afternoon begins, and its last time is when the sun sets, and the first time for the afternoon Maghrib is when the sun sets, and the last of its time is when the horizon disappears, and the beginning of the time for the last evening prayer is when the horizon disappears. And the last of its time is when the middle of the night, and the beginning of the time of dawn is when the dawn appears, and the last of its time is when The sun rises. (Tirmidhi 151. Ahmad 2/232)"
"3242","(3242) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, he will pray the afternoon prayer that you called the first time when the sun sets, and he will pray the afternoon prayer, then one of us will return to He traveled to the farthest part of the city while the sun was still alive. He said: And I forgot what he said in Morocco. He said: He liked to He would delay the evening prayer, which you call Al-Atama, and he would stop from the morning prayer when the man recognized his companion, and he would It is read from sixty to one hundred. (Muslim 2371, Abu Dawud 401)"
"3243","(3243) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Hassan, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the noon prayer in the afternoon prayer, and the afternoon prayer while the sun was pure, and the sunset prayer when It is obligatory, and the evening meal is sometimes delayed and sometimes hastened. If he sees them gathered, he hurries it, and when he sees them they delay it. He delayed it, and in the morning, he said: They were, or he said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to lead her in prayer with a bath. \n(Bukhari 560, Muslim 233)"
"3244","(3244) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the Fajr prayer? So he ordered Bilal to call the call to prayer when dawn came, then the next day when he left, then he said: Where is the questioner? Between that time."
"3245","(3245) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Kharijiya bin Abdullah bin Sulaiman bin Zayd bin Thabit told me, he said: Hussein bin Bashir bin Salman told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I and Muhammad bin Ali, or a man from Ali’s family, entered Ali. Jabir bin Abdullah, so we said to him: Tell us how was the prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the afternoon prayer when the shade was like a trap, then he led us in the afternoon prayer when the shade was The same and the example of Shirak, then he led us in the Maghrib prayer when the sun had set, then he led us in the evening prayer when twilight had set, then he led us in the prayer Fajr when dawn came, then he led us in prayer the next day at noon when everything was in the same shade, then he led us in the afternoon prayer when it was Everything remained in the same shade as long as the rider walked to the one with the neck, then he led the Maghrib prayer with us when the sun set. Then he led us in the evening prayer when a third of the night had passed, then he led us in the dawn prayer and continued. So we said to him: How can we pray with the pilgrims when he delays? He said: He did not pray at the time, then pray with him. If he delayed it, they prayed it at the time, and made it with him as a voluntary prayer, and hadith. This is a guarantee for you. If I die, if the pilgrims are able to dig me up, let them dig me up. (Nasa’i 524)"
"3246","(3246) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, he said: Bashir bin Abi Masoud informed me, on the authority of His father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Gabriel came down and gave him security, until he counted five prayers. (Bukhari 521, Muslim 425)"
"3247","(3247) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, he said: I heard Abu Ayyub speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: The time of noon, as long as the time of the afternoon has not come, and the time of the afternoon, as long as the sun has not yet set, and the time of sunset, as long as a bull has not fallen. Twilight, evening time until midnight, and morning time unless the sun rises."
"3248","(3248) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, he said: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abd God Ibn Amr said: He did not raise it twice, then raised it, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said; Then he mentioned something like the hadith of Gandar.\n(Muslim 427. Ahmad 2/213)"
"3249","(3249) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn al-Nu`man, on the authority of Ali ibn Amr, who said: The letter of Umar came to us: They prayed the dawn while the stars were shining brightly, and they prayed the noon prayer when the sun had disappeared from the middle of the sky, and they prayed the afternoon prayer while the sun was white. They are pure, they prayed the Maghrib prayer when the sun sets, and they made a concession for the evening prayer."
"3250","(3250) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, who said: Omar wrote to Abu Musa: Pray the noon prayer when the sun has passed, pray the afternoon prayer while the sun is bright and bright, and pray the sunset prayer when the night is mixed. And the day, pray the evening prayer at any time you wish, and pray the dawn prayer when the light shines."
"3251","(3251) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Al-Zahir is like its name. And the afternoon, and the sun is bright and bright, and Morocco is like its name. We used to pray Morocco with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then we would come to our homes about a mile away and see the locations of the arrows. He used to hasten the evening prayer and delay it, and dawn was like its name. And he used to wash with her. (Ahmed 3/303, Abd al-Razzaq 2091)"
"3252","(3252) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: They were believing women. They pray the morning prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then they return to their families and no one recognizes them.\n(Bukhari 5788 Muslim 231)"
"3253","(3253) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, will lead the dawn prayer, and then the women of the believers will come out, wrapped in their cloaks, of what they know is covered with shame."
"3254","(3254) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Al-Muhajir informed me, he said: I read Omar’s letter to Abu Musa said that there are times for prayer, so when he finished until dawn, or he said: until lunch, he said: Stand there in darkness, or Slowly, and prolong the recitation."
"3255","(3255) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Mansour bin Hayyan told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Maymun al-Awdi He says: If I were to pray Fajr behind Omar ibn al-Khattab, even if he were three cubits taller than me, I would not even recognize him. He speaks"
"3256","(3256) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to Abdul Al-Hamid: To be anointed with dawn."
"3257","(3257) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, on the authority of Abu Salman, who said: I served the riders in the time of Uthman, and people used to wash them. At dawn."
"3258","(3258) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, on the authority of his father; That Abu Musa prayed the dawn prayer in darkness."
"3259","(3259) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar; He prayed with Ibn al-Zubayr, and he used to wash his hands at dawn, and he would leave and we did not know each other."
"3260","(3260) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Iyas al-Hanafi told me, on the authority of his father, he said We used to pray Fajr with Othman, then we would leave, but we would not know each other’s faces."
"3261","(3261) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Travel at dawn, for it is greater in reward.\n(Abu Dawud 427 Ahmad 3/140)"
"3262","(3262) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, who said: We used to pray the dawn prayer and it would be recited. Our imam recited the surah from the Meen and we were wearing our clothes. Then we brought Ibn Masoud and found him praying."
"3263","(3263) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Ubaid, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah; Ali said: O son of Al-Nabah, break out at dawn."
"3264","(3264) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; That Ibn Masoud used to light the dawn at dawn."
"3265","(3265) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Ruq, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Muqti’, who said: I saw Al-Hussein bin Ali walking at dawn. Very"
"3266","(3266) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubair bin Nufayr, who said: Mu'awiyah led us in prayer with a deep voice, so Abu Darda' said: Travel with this prayer, for it is the most understanding of you."
"3267","(3267) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Radhi bin Abi Aqeel, on the authority of his father, who said: Rabi’ bin Jubayr used to say And his muezzin said: O Abu Aqeel, lighten, lighten."
"3268","(3268) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: He was Ibn Masoud. He enlightens with the dawn."
"3269","(3269) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Hind; Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to travel at dawn."
"3270","(3270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to travel at dawn."
"3271","(3271) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to bring light at dawn."
"3272","(3272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: Travel at dawn, for the more you travel, the greater the reward. (Tahawi 179)"
"3273","(3273) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: They used to like to leave the morning prayer, and one of them He sees the location of his arrow."
"3274","(3274) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Bishr bin Urwa, he said: I traveled with Alqamah, and he used to shine in the morning."
"3275","(3275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were not unanimously agreed. He greeted me on something, but they agreed upon the light of dawn."
"3276","(3276) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Nafa`i ibn Muslim, who said: Suwayd ibn Ghafla used to travel at dawn."
"3277","(3277) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqa’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to bring light at dawn."
"3278","(3278) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of a man; Some of Abdullah’s companions used to travel with the dawn prayer."
"3279","(3279) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Kharshia, who said: Omar led the people in the dawn prayer and sat down. He enlightened and led them in prayer in between."
"3280","(3280) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba prayed. In the morning, it rose and lit, until I said: Has the sun risen or not? And he prayed in between, and his muezzin was Ibn al-Nabah. And there was no muezzin other than him."
"3281","(3281) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sadus, a man from the neighborhood; The spring said: Light, light."
"3282","(3282) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rukin Al-Dhabi, who said: I heard Tamim bin Hudhalam, and he was one of the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: Light, light with prayer."
"3283","(3283) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha She said: I have not seen anyone who was more hastening to appear than the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, nor Abu Bakr, nor Omar.\n(Tirmidhi 155. Ahmad 6/135)"
"3284","(3284) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar used to pray the noon prayer when the sun had set."
"3285","(3285) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah bin led in prayer for us. Masoud prayed at noon when the sun had passed the zenith, then he said: This, by the One besides Whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer."
"3286","(3286) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: When the sun had set, Abu Musa came and said: Where? Your friend? This is the time for this prayer, and it was not long before Abdullah came quickly and prayed the noon prayer."
"3287","(3287) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Abu Al-Minhal told me, he said: I went with my father to Abi Barza. He said: Tell us how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the prescribed prayer? He said: He used to pray the Hajir prayer that you call “Al-Awla” when the sun sets."
"3288","(3288) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, Umm Salama said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is more hastening the appearance than you, and you are more delaying the afternoon than he is. \n(Tirmidhi 163. Ahmad 6/310)"
"3289","(3289) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Shihab, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Abu Hurairah About noon time? He said: If the sun has set at midday, and the shadow has measured the roofs, then noon has risen."
"3290","(3290) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Maimoon ibn Miran narrated to me; Suwayd bin Ghaflali used to pray the noon prayer when the sun had set, so the pilgrims sent to him: “Do not precede us in our prayer.” Suwayd said. : I prayed it with Abu Bakr and Omar like this, and death is too close to me for me to pray for it."
"3291","(3291) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: It was Omar leaves the Hijra in the heat, then he goes to Quba and finds them praying."
"3292","(3292) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: It was Bilal gives the call to prayer when the sun sets. (Muslim 1888, Abu Dawud 406)"
"3293","(3293) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Wahhab, on the authority of Khabab, who said: We complained to the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him during Ramadan, and He did not complain to us. (Muslim 1898, Ahmad 5/108)"
"3294","(3294) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: I was praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon, so I took a handful of pebbles and put them on my palm, then I shift it to the other hand until it cools, then I place it on my forehead when I prostrate, because of the extreme heat.\n(Abu Dawud 402. Ahmad 3/327)"
"3295","(3295) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: We used to pray the noon prayer with him sometimes. We find shade to sit in, and sometimes we do not find shade to sit in."
"3296","(3296) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Khushaf ibn Malik, he said: Abdullah led us in prayer. And the grasshoppers jump because of the intensity of the rain."
"3297","(3297) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, he said: I asked my father, I said: I prayed with Ali, so tell me how it was. He prays the noon prayer? He said: When the sun has passed the zenith."
"3298","(3298) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: I asked Jafar about the time of noon? He said: When the sun has passed the zenith, then he said: You should listen, because for a man to delay it until he prays the afternoon prayer is better for him than for him to pray it. Before the sun goes down."
"3299","(3299) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Cool off with prayer, meaning noon, for the intensity of the heat is from the stench of Hell.\n(Bukhari 3259. Ahmad 3/59)"
"3300","(3300) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Cool down with prayer, for the heat of the afternoon is from the stench of Hell. (Bukhari 5361, Muslim 430)"
"3301","(3301) Shabab bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Al-Muhajir Abu Al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: I heard Zaid bin Wahhab He narrates, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey and Bilal wanted to give the call to prayer. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Cool down. Then he wanted to give the call to prayer, so he said: Cool down, until we saw a fire. Al-Tawlul, then he gave the call to prayer and the noon prayer, then he said: The heat is intense because of the blazing heat of Hell, so when the heat becomes intense, cool off with prayer.\n(Bukhari 5350, Muslim 431)"
"3302","(3302) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Abu Musa, He used to say: Cool down with prayer."
"3303","(3303) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Sabit, who said: Abu Mahdhura called for prayer. At noon in Mecca, Omar said to him: Is it your voice, O Abu Mahdhurah, that I heard? He said: Yes, I have stored it for you, O Commander of the Faithful, so that I may listen to you. Omar said: O Abu Mahdhuriya, you are in a difficult land."
"3304","(3304) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The heat, or the intensity of the heat from the stench of Hell, so they were cooled by the appearance."
"3305","(3305) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, saying: Bashir bin Salman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Safwan, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Cool off with the noon prayer, for the heat is intense from the stench of Hell.\n(Bukhari 2923. Ahmad 4/262)"
"3306","(3306) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail, on the authority of Qays, he said: It used to be said: Cool down in the afternoon, for the gates of Hell are It opens."
"3307","(3307) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Mundhir, he said: Omar said: Refer to the afternoon, for The intensity of heat from the stench of Hell."
"3308","(3308) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Kathir bin Mudarik, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Zaid said: Abdullah said: At the beginning of the time of noon, you should look at your feet and measure three to five feet. Feet, and the beginning of the final time is five to seven feet. I think he said: in the winter."
"3309","(3309) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, who said: They used to pray the noon prayer while the shadow stood."
"3310","(3310) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The zuhr prayer is performed when there is shade. Three cubits, and if she hastened a pilgrim, he would pray before that, and if he was busy with something, he would pray after that, Zaidah said: I said to Mansour: Doesn’t that only mean in the summer? He said: Yes."
"3311","(3311) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: When a man’s shadow was three Adhar' is the time for the noon prayer."
"3312","(3312) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I prayed with Ibn Umar and wanted to measure his prayer, so I understood. I divided it and found it to be three cubits long."
"3313","(3313) Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Harith bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, saying: I asked Muhammad bin Sirin about the time for the prayer. Noon? He said: If its shade is three cubits, then that is when you pray the noon prayer."
"3314","(3314) Al-Fadl bin[corrupt] narrated to us. Dukain, he said: Harith bin Al-Sa’ib told us, he said: I asked Al-Hasan about the time of noon? He said: If the fay is removed from the length of the thing, then that is when you pray the noon prayer."
"3315","(3315) Waki’ and Muadh narrated to us, both on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Time is not extended. Like a trap, whoever makes a mistake will be destroyed."
"3316","(3316) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He is praying the afternoon prayer while the sun is rising in your room, and the fay has not yet appeared. (Bukhari 522, Abu Dawud 410)"
"3317","(3317) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, on the authority of Abu Al-Abyad, on the authority of Anas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying the afternoon prayer while the sun was white, then he came to my clan on the side of They did not pray in Medina, so I say: Why are you sitting? Pray, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed.\n(Ahmad 3/232, Daraqutni 10)"
"3318","(3318) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdou, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, who said: I wrote to Omar May I ask him about the time of the afternoon prayer? So he wrote to me to pray the afternoon prayer when the sun is between the two slits."
"3319","(3319) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was white. Pure, He hastens it once, and delays it at the end."
"3320","(3320) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: You pray the afternoon prayer while the sun is bright, and its life is that You will find her heat."
"3321","(3321) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abu Al-Najashi, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: We used to pray with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then we slaughter the camels, divide them into ten parts, then we cook and eat meat. mature before we pray the Maghrib prayer. (Bukhari 2480, Muslim 435)"
"3322","(3322) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, he said: I asked my father, I said: I prayed with Ali, so he told me how it was. He performs the afternoon prayer? He said: He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was high."
"3323","(3323) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: A man came to Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah, and he was on Kufa, and he saw him delaying the afternoon prayer, so he said to him: Why do you delay the afternoon prayer? I used to pray it with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then I would return to my family, to Banu Amr bin Awf. And the sun is high."
"3324","(3324) Shababih narrated to us, he said: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He used to pray the afternoon prayer while the sun was high, so the one who was going would go and the high calamities would come while the sun was high.\n(Muslim 1921, Abu Dawud 407)"
"3325","(3325) - Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to me, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Abu Waqid, on the authority of Abu Arwa, who said: I was praying with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the afternoon, then he came to the tree, meaning Dhul-Halif, before the sun had set (Tahawi 191)"
"3326","(3326) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulkiah; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the afternoon prayer, then he took out money to divide it and hasten to spend the night."
"3327","(3327) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abi Asim, on the authority of Abi Aoun; That Ali used to delay the afternoon prayer until the sun rose over the walls."
"3328","(3328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Munabbih, on the authority of Siwar ibn Shabib, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He used to delay the afternoon prayer until I would say: The sun has turned yellow."
"3329","(3329) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, and Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, On the authority of Abdullah; He used to delay the afternoon prayer."
"3330","(3330) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The son of my brother Al-Aswad was their muezzin, so he was He hastened the afternoon prayer, and Al-Aswad said to him: Either you will obey us in our call to prayer, or you will isolate yourself from our muezzins."
"3331","(3331) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There were those before you who delayed the afternoon prayer more severely than you."
"3332","(3332) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Waki`, who said: Abraham said to me: Do not perform the afternoon prayer until you do not hear those around you. muezzin."
"3333","(3333) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I came to Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, and he He performed ablution and said: The knitters have overpowered our prayer and hastened it, meaning the afternoon prayer."
"3334","(3334) Jarir narrated to us on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, who said: The afternoon prayer is as far as the caravan travels a farsakh until sunset."
"3335","(3335) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Mardanaba, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid, who said: I asked Anas about the time of the afternoon prayer. ? He said: Its time is to travel six miles until the sun sets."
"3336","(3336) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Harish, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: You pray the afternoon prayer when the shadow is one. Twenty feet in winter and summer."
"3337","(3337) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: It was named Al-Asr to squeeze it."
"3338","(3338) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: We used to pray the Maghrib prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. Then we brought Banu Salama, and one of us saw the location of his nobility. (Abu Dawud 419. Ibn Khuzaymah 338)"
"3339","(3339) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Al-Najashi narrated to us, he said: Rafi’ narrated to us Ibn Khadij, he said: We used to pray the Maghrib prayer at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and one of us would leave. To look at the sites of his nobility. (Bukhari 598, Muslim 441)"
"3340","(3340) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwaid bin Ghafla, who said: Omar said: Pray this prayer. Al-Fajjaj is Misfirah, which means Morocco."
"3341","(3341) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar used to write to the princes of the cities not to Wait for your prayers for the clash of stars."
"3342","(3342) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah used to pray the Maghrib prayer when it set. The sun and says: This, and there is no god but Him, the time for this prayer."
"3343","(3343) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Bishr, who said: Ibn al-Hanafi was the muezzin. He calls the Maghrib call to prayer whenever the sun sets at the same time."
"3344","(3344) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy; That Suwayd bin Ghafli used to order his muezzin to call the Maghrib call to prayer when the sun set."
"3345","(3345) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj al-Sawaf, on the authority of Abdullah al-Danaj, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. They struggle after sunset."
"3346","(3346) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Hajib bin Omar, who said: I used to hear my uncle Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj asking Abu Hind for a dirham. About this hadith? Dirham says: I was coming from the market and people would meet me as they were leaving. Maqil bin Yassar had led them in prayer, but I was leaving. The sun, or has it not set?"
"3347","(3347) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas Amr bin Marwan, he said: I asked my father, I said: You prayed with Ali. So tell me how he used to pray the Maghrib prayer? He said: He would pray when the disc fell."
"3348","(3348) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of a man who I think he said: From the sons of the captains, On the authority of his father, he said: We used to pray the Maghrib prayer with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then we would return to our camps and one of us would see. The locations of the arrows. He said: I said to Al-Zuhri: How far were their homes from Medina? He said: Two-thirds of a mile. (Tabarani 117)"
"3349","(3349) Shababi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Saleh, the client of the twins, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid, he said: We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would go to the market, and if an arrow was shot, I would see. Their locations\n(Ahmad 4/115 Tabarani 5260)"
"3350","(3350) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidiya, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I prayed with Abdullah Al-Maghrib, the extent to which if a man shoots an arrow, he will see its location."
"3351","(3351) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Habib, that he reported to him on the authority of Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Pray the Maghrib prayer when the fasting person breaks his fast. He hastened to do so. The rising of the stars. (Tabarani 4083)"
"3352","(3352) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He delays the last dinner. (Muslim 226. Ahmad 5/89)"
"3353","(3353) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, he said: I am the one who knows best. people, or like the most knowledgeable of people about the time for the Isha prayer) The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray it after the fall of The moon on the second night of the beginning of the month. (Tirmidhi 1651, Ahmad 4/270)"
"3354","(3354) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barza, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, it is desirable to delay the evening meal, which people call “the dark night.”"
"3355","(3355) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. He hastens the evening meal and delays it."
"3356","(3356) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to us, on the authority of Urwa; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the evening prayer when the horizon was dark, and sometimes he delayed it until the people had gathered. \n(Abu Dawud 397. Ibn Khuzaymah 352)"
"3357","(3357) Ibn al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Labiba, he said: Abu said to me Here: Pray the Isha prayer when twilight has gone and the night has darkened between you and a third of the night, and you have not hastened after the white of the night has gone. The horizon is better."
"3358","(3358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Omar wrote to Abu Musa to pray the Isha’ prayer until a third of the night. If you delay it, then for half the night, and do not be among the heedless."
"3359","(3359) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: He was Ibn Masoud. He delays dinner."
"3360","(3360) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The time for the final night prayer is a quarter of the night."
"3361","(3361) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr bin Marwan, he said: I asked my father, I said: I prayed with Ali, so tell me how it was. Does he pray the evening prayer? He said: When the twilight disappears."
"3362","(3362) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Bard, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: Isha time until a third of the night, no sleep, no heedlessness."
"3363","(3363) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We waited for the night before the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for the last evening prayer, until a third of the night had passed, or later, then He came out to us, and I do not know what his business or need was with his family, so he said: I do not know the people of religion. Others are waiting for this prayer, and had I not made it difficult for your nation, I would have led this prayer with them in this hour. (Bukhari 570, Abu Dawud 423)"
"3364","(3364) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have delayed the evening prayer until a third of the night, or Midnight. (Ibn Majah 691)"
"3365","(3365) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hariz told us, he said: Rashid bin Saad told us, on the authority of Asim bin Hamid. Al-Sakouni, who was one of the companions of Muadh, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, said: We stayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in prayer. Even the evening prayer was delayed, until someone said: He had prayed but did not go out, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out to us. And the speaker says: O Messenger of God, we thought that you prayed and did not go out, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Cover yourselves. With this prayer, you have been favored over all other nations, and no nation prayed it before you.\n(Abu Dawud 424. Ahmad 5/237)"
"3366","(3366) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the evening prayer one night, so he went out while his head was dripping and said: Were it not that I would be too hard Upon my nation, I have made the time for this prayer this time. (Darimi 1215. Ibn Hibban 1533)"
"3367","(3367) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Amr bin Damra narrated to us, on the authority of A man from Jehanna said: He said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when should I perform the evening prayer? He said: When night fills the depths of every valley. (Ahmad 5/365)"
"3368","(3368) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaid, on the authority of his father, who said: We used to pray with al-Nu’man, meaning Ibn Bashir, Maghrib, and when the last of us leaves, he begins to eat dinner."
"3369","(3369) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, he said: He said: Omar: Hurry up for dinner before the worker becomes lazy and the sick person falls asleep."
"3370","(3370) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The heaviest prayers for the hypocrites are the evening prayers and the dawn prayers, and if they knew what is in them, they would have performed them even if They crawled, and I was about to order the prayer, and it would be performed, then I would order a man, and he would lead the people in prayer, then I would go with some men, with them. He sent bundles of firewood to a people who did not attend prayer, and their houses were burned with fire.\n(Bukhari 657, Abu Dawud 549)"
"3371","(3371) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith, on the authority of Abu Basir, he said: My father said Ibn Ka'b: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led us in prayer. When he finished the prayer, he saw a small number of the people of the mosque, and he said: Did so-and-so witness? We said: Yes, until he counted three people and said: There is no prayer heavier for the hypocrites than the last evening prayer. The Fajr prayer. If they knew what was in them, they would have come to them even if they had crawled. (Abu Dawud 5550, Ahmad 5/140)"
"3372","(3372) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya Bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If we were lost The man in the evening and dawn prayers, we have a bad suspicion of him."
"3373","(3373) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu Umair bin Anas, he said: He told me My cousins from the Ansar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no hypocrite who speaks to them, meaning the evening and dawn prayers.\n(Ahmed 5/57, Abdul Razzaq 2023)"
"3374","(3374) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Darda’; He said during his illness in which he died: “Don’t you carry me?” He said: “So they carried him and took him out.” He said: “Listen, and inform those who Behind you: observe these two prayers; Evening and morning, and if you knew what is in them, you would have come to them even if you had crawled on your elbows and knees."
"3375","(3375) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Yuhannis said that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If only people knew what is in virtue The evening prayer and the morning prayer will come to them even if they crawl. (Ahmad 6/80, An-Nasa’i 386)"
"3376","(3376) Abdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Amr al-Ansari He said: I came while Othman was sitting in the mosque during the last evening prayer, so I sat next to him, and Othman said: Witnesses of the morning prayer. Such as standing up for the night, and the evening prayer is like standing up for half the night."
"3377","(3377) Shababi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Omar, he said: Because It is more beloved to me to pray them together than to revive what was between them."
"3378","(3378) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr. \n(H) And Shu`bah, on the authority of Najiya bin Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Omar, who said: Because I attend the evening and dawn prayers in A group of people is dearer to me than to revive what is between them."
"3379","(3379) Abdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, who said: Omar was He came down from the market and Al-Shifa’ bin Abdullah passed by. He passed by her one day during Ramadan and said: Where is Sulaiman? Her son. She said: He is sleeping. He said: What did he witness for the morning prayer? She said: No, he stood up with the people at night, then came and hit his head, and Omar said: Witnessing the morning prayer is more beloved to me than standing. night until dawn."
"3380","(3380) Zaid narrated to us on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Because I attend the evening and dawn prayers in congregation is more beloved to me than He revived what was between them."
"3381","(3381) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The red twilight."
"3382","(3382) Ibn Numayr and Waki` told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit and Shaddad ibn Aws were They pray the last Isha prayer if the red color is absent."
"3383","(3383) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Hawshab, he said: I said to Mujahid: Al-Shafq. He said: Do not say Al-Shafq, for Al-Shafq is one of the The sun, but say the redness of the horizon."
"3384","(3384) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Fudayl bin Marzuq told us, he said: I asked Jabir al-Ja’fi about These verses: “Until the white thread becomes distinct to you from the black thread of dawn”? He said: Saeed bin Jubayr said: It is the redness of the horizons."
"3385","(3385) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is a time between every two prayers."
"3386","(3386) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no time between prayer and prayer."
"3387","(3387) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mundhir, who said: I asked Mary Abu Razin when will you miss a prayer? He said: Do not miss a prayer until the time for the next prayer begins, but in between that is negligence and neglect."
"3388","(3388) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Asbagh, who said: I heard Ibn Abbas many times saying: Do not miss a prayer. He even calls for the Hereafter."
"3389","(3389) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uthman ibn Mawhib, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah being asked: What is negligence? In prayer? He said: To delay it until the time for the next prayer comes."
"3390","(3390) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, who said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he was delivered to the Holy House, for sixteen months until the verses concerning Al-Baqarah were revealed: {And wherever you are, flee. And your faces were divided into two parts. It was revealed after the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had prayed, and a man from the people set off and passed by people from the Ansar. While they were praying, he told them the hadith, so they turned their faces towards the House. (Muslim 11. Tirmidhi 2962)"
"3391","(3391) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Jamil bin Ubaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Thumama, on the authority of his grandfather Anas bin Malik, who said: A caller from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: The direction of the Qiblah has been turned to the Sacred House of God, and the imam has prayed."
"3392","(3392) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God prayed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his companions to the Holy House for sixteen months, then the Qiblah was made afterward. (Ahmad 1/250)"
"3393","(3393) Shababi told us, he said: Qays told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Alaqi, on the authority of Amara bin Aws, he said: We used to pray to The Holy House, when someone came to us while our imam was bowing, and we were bowing, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has been revealed. The Qur’an was upon him, and he was commanded to face the Ka’bah, or not, so face it. He said: Then our imam turned aside while he was bowing, and turned away. The people until they faced the Kaaba, so we prayed some of that prayer facing the Holy House, and some of it facing the Kaaba.\n(Abu Ali 1509. Ibn Saad 243)"
"3394","(3394) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn Shihab; He was asked about a people who prayed on a cloudy day facing other than the direction of direction, then the direction of direction became clear to them while they were praying? He said: They face the Qiblah and repeat the 'iddah as long as they prayed. The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did that at the time. They were ordered to face the Kaaba, and in prayer they were praying to the Holy House, so they faced the Kaaba, so they prayed. Some of that prayer leads to the Holy House, and some of it leads to the Kaaba."
"3395","(3395) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: They were bowing in Fajr prayer, so they turned aside while bowing."
"3396","(3396) Waki` narrated to us, saying: An-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, saying: I heard Mujahid saying: {So wherever you turn, there is the face of God} He said: May God accept it, so wherever you are, east or west, face it."
"3397","(3397) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Sinan Abu Sinan, who said: I heard al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim saying: (And for every person there is a face. Her Master) He says: To every person he is his Master."
"3398","(3398) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mas’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Simak al-Hanafi, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas saying: Do not make any of The House is left behind, and he completes it completely."
"3399","(3399) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: {Shatrah}: meeting him."
"3400","(3400) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who prays on a cloudy day in a direction other than that, he said: That is sufficient."
"3401","(3401) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who prayed on a cloudy day, but then he prayed on a different day. The kiss? He said: It is sufficient. He said: Someone who asked Ibrahim and Al-Shu’bi told me, and they said: It is sufficient."
"3402","(3402) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Yazid, he said: I prayed while I was blind for more than one reason. Qiblah, so I asked Abraham? He said: It will suffice for you."
"3403","(3403) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who prays for someone other than the tribe? He said: It is sufficient."
"3404","(3404) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who prays in a direction other than the qiblah, he said, “That is sufficient.”"
"3405","(3405) Waki’ told us, he said: Mis’ar told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is sufficient."
"3406","(3406) Wakī’ narrated to us, Ibn Abi Arouba narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’eed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: There is no retaliation for him."
"3407","(3407) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man prays on a cloudy day other than the direction of prayer, then The clouds have opened and you have prayed some of your prayers, so be rewarded for what you prayed, then turn your face towards the direction of prayer."
"3408","(3408) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who prayed in a direction other than the qiblah, he said: His prayer has ended."
"3409","(3409) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman prayed in our house, so I said To him: Indeed, there is ease in our qiblah, so he repeated it."
"3410","(3410) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He celebrates the feast."
"3411","(3411) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever prays in a direction other than the direction of prayer, then he wakes up. And it is in a time, then he has to repeat it, but if it is not in a time, then he does not have to repeat it."
"3412","(3412) Waki’ told us, he said: Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He celebrates as long as there is time."
"3413","(3413) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Marthad, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan; He hated for them to say: The time for prayer has come."
"3414","(3414) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate it. They say: The time for prayer has come, and he said: The time for prayer has not come, and they say: The time for prayer has come."
"3415","(3415) Al-Muttalib bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; He was waiting when he heard the footsteps of a shoe."
"3416","(3416) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If you were an imam and someone entered while you were bowing, So wait for him."
"3417","(3417) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If one of you comes while the imam is bowing, Let him walk quickly, for we are waiting for him."
"3418","(3418) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He was waiting when he heard the footsteps of sandals."
"3419","(3419) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abi Awfa; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was waiting when he heard the footsteps of a sandal."
"3420","(3420) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; He was waiting when he heard the footsteps of a shoe."
"3421","(3421) Hushaym told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the One day, he saw a rope stretched out, and he said: What is this? It was said: So-and-so prays, O Messenger of God, and when she is tired, she can rest on this rope. He said: Let her pray as long as she is tired. You are tired, let you sleep. (Ahmad 184; Abu Ali 3786)"
"3422","(3422) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of his mistress, she said: I was among the companions of the class. We had ropes to which we could hang when we grew tired and drowsy during prayer, and rugs to lay on because of the thickness of the earth. She said: Then Abu came to him. Bakr, and he said: Cut these ropes and go to the ground."
"3423","(3423) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of a man who named him, and Abu Bakr thinks it is: Amr ibn Murah, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Only the Jews do that, meaning by hanging from below like this."
"3424","(3424) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Asim bin Shumaikh, who said: I saw Abu Sa`id al-Khudri praying. Leaning on a staff."
"3425","(3425) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, he said: Tell me who saw Abu Dharr praying. Leaning on a staff."
"3426","(3426) Hafs and Yazid told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They lean on the stick during prayer. Yazid increased: when they were equal."
"3427","(3427) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Amr ibn Maimun had a stake installed in the wall of the mosque. And if he was tired of standing during prayer, or it was difficult for him, he would hold on to the peg and rely on it."
"3428","(3428) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, he said: I saw a woman, and he was leading his people in prayer, and I saw He has a strength that he can rely on when he gets up."
"3429","(3429) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Araak bin Malik, on the authority of his father, he said: I caught the people in During the month of Ramadan, ropes are tied for them, and they will cling to them for the duration of the qiyam."
"3430","(3430) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, who said: I saw Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa praying, reclining. Ali is disobedient."
"3431","(3431) Ibn Aliyah and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Fatima, his son The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, he would say: In the name of God. And peace be upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he departs, He said: In the name of God, and peace be upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. O God, forgive me my sins and open the doors of Thank you (Tirmidhi 314, Ahmad 6/283)"
"3432","(3432) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Amr Al-Madini, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abd Allah bin Hantab; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered the mosque, he would say: O God, open for me the doors of Your mercy, and make it easy for me. The doors of your livelihood."
"3433","(3433) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ali, who said: When he enters the mosque, He said: O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. And when he left, he said: O God, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy. Doors of your grace"
"3434","(3434) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: According to Kaab bin Ajra: When you enter the mosque, greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: O God, open the doors for me. Your mercy, and when you leave, greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: Oh God, protect me from Satan."
"3435","(3435) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd The Most Gracious; When Abdullah bin Salam entered the mosque, he would greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and say: Oh God, open the doors for me. Your mercy, and when he goes out, he greets the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and seeks refuge from Satan."
"3436","(3436) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Dhu Haddan, on the authority of Alqamiya; When he entered the mosque, he would say: Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and may God’s mercy and blessings be upon him. May God’s blessings and angels be upon him. Muhammad"
"3437","(3437) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he entered the mosque, he would say: In the name of God and peace be upon the Messenger of God. God, and when he enters a house where there is no one, he says: Peace be upon you."
"3438","(3438) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amer bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Qatada; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If you enter the mosque, pray two rak’ahs before you sit down.\n(Bukhari 444 and Muslim 495)"
"3439","(3439) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abd al-A’la ibn al-Hakam, on the authority of Kharijiya ibn al-Salt al-Burjami, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It used to be said: from approaching, or from signs, that seeks for the mosques to take roads."
"3440","(3440) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abi Amr bin Hamas, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadith Al-Nadhari, on the authority of Abu Dharr; He entered the mosque, came to a pole, and prayed two rak'ahs there."
"3441","(3441) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abi Qatada The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Give the mosques their right. It was said: What is their right? He said: Two rak'ahs before you sit down."
"3442","(3442) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Khashshash, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in the mosque, and he said to me: O Abu Dharr, did you pray? I said: No, he said: Then stand up and pray two rak’ahs. (Ahmad 1798, Talisi 478)"
"3443","(3443) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn"
"3444","(3444) Abbad told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; What about a man entering a mosque and praying there whenever he passes by? He said: He prays two rak'ahs, then spends the rest of his day in it."
"3445","(3445) Harami bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, he said: I saw Ikrim entering the mosque and praying there. Two rak'ahs, and he said: This is the right of the mosque."
"3446","(3446) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: I came to the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him while he was in the mosque, and he said: Pray two rak’ahs. (Bukhari 443. Muslim 495)"
"3447","(3447) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They enter the mosque, then they leave and do not pray. He said: And I saw Ibn Umar doing that."
"3448","(3448) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar used to pass by the mosque but would not pray in it."
"3449","3449) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I passed with Al-Sha’biyyah in the Kufa Mosque, and I said to him: No. Do you pray? He said: Then, by my Lord, we will continue to pray."
"3450","(3450) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Hanash, he said: I saw Suwayd bin Ghafla passing by our mosque, so perhaps he prayed. And perhaps he did not pray."
"3451","(3451) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw a man entering from the mosque until he came out. Of peaches, one should not pray in them."
"3452","(3452) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (h) and Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Jubayr; They disliked making noise during prayer when the imam mentioned a sign of mercy, or a sign of punishment, or the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned May God bless him and grant him peace."
"3453","(3453) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The best place to stand is the mosque. Then the right of the mosque."
"3454","(3454) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is desirable for the imam to take the oath."
"3455","(3455) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; It was astonishing for him to stand at the right hand of the Imam."
"3456","(3456) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Salama bin Abi Yahya, who said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab praying in the cleft. The right side of the mosque."
"3457","(3457) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Salama bin Abi Yahya, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik praying in the left side of The mosque"
"3458","(3458) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran Al-Manqari, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They were praying on the left side of the Imam."
"3459","(3459) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Ibn al-Bara’, on the authority of his father, who said: We used to love or We desire to stand at the right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 304, Muslim 62)"
"3460","(3460) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The right-hand sides of the rows are five more than the rest of the mosque. And twenty degrees."
"3461","(3461) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, who narrated it, saying: The one who misses the afternoon prayer, It is as if he was keeping his family and wealth close to him. (Muslim 436. Ahmad 2/134)"
"3462","(3462) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who He left the afternoon prayer until the sun had set without an excuse, as if he had left his family and property behind. (Bukhari 552. Muslim 5/439)"
"3463","(3463) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak, on the authority of Nawfal bin Muawiyah bin Urwah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Among the prayers is the prayer of one who misses it, as if it were a Witr prayer. His family and wealth. Ibn Omar said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: This is the afternoon prayer.\n(Bukhari 3602, Ahmed 422)"
"3464","(3464) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abbad bin Misra Al-Manqari informed us, on the authority of Abu Qalabab and Al-Hasan: They were sitting, and Abu Qalababi said: Abu Darda’ said: Whoever neglects the afternoon prayer until it is missed without an excuse, has failed. He did it, he said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever abandons an obligatory prayer until you miss it without an excuse, has His work was ruined.\n(Ahmad 6/442)"
"3465","(3465) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: Whoever missed the afternoon prayer, It is as if he had been linked to his family."
"3466","(3466) Abu Asama narrated to us, he said: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Suleiman bin Dawud was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, does not speak out of respect for him, as the afternoon prayer passed, and no one was able to speak to him."
"3467","(3467) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, he said: I was informed that he was one of the The afternoon missed him, as if he had left his family and wealth behind."
"3468","(3468) Issa bin Yunus and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Buraida Al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever missed it The afternoon prayer is invalidated. (Ibn Majah 694. Ahmad 5/361)"
"3469","(3469) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Buraidah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like the hadith of Jesus and Waki’. (Bukhari 594. Ahmad 5/357)"
"3470","(3470) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of Aws bin Damaj, on the authority of Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The one who recites the Book of God will lead the people in prayer, for if they are all alike in the recitation. So I am the most knowledgeable of them in the Sunnah, and if they are all the same in the Sunnah, then I am the most knowledgeable of them in the Hijra, if they are all in the Hijra. So he advanced to them in peace, and no man believes in his authority, nor does he sit in his house on his own honour, except With His permission\n(Muslim 690. Abu Dawud 3/583)"
"3471","(3471) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If there are three of them, then one of them should lead them, and the one most worthy of the imamate should lead them. I read to them.\n(Muslim 464. Ahmad 36)"
"3472","(3472) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Zayd bin Iyas, who said: Murā bin Sharāhil narrated to us, who said: I was There was a house in which there were Abdullah bin Masoud, Hudhayfy, and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, and the time for prayer came, and this man said to this man: He came forward, and said: This is to this: He came forward, and Abdullah was between Abu Musa and Hudhayfah, so they took him towards me and they brought him forward. I said: What is that for? He said: He witnessed Badr."
"3473","(3473) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Salem was leading the Muhajireen and Ansar in Quba Mosque"
"3474","(3474) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Asim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Salamah, he said: When my people returned from the Messenger of May God bless him and grant him peace. They said to him: Indeed, he said to us: The one among you who has recited the Qur’an the most. He said: So they called him. So they taught me to bow and prostrate, and I used to lead them in prayer while wearing a loose cloak. He said: They used to say to my father: “Won’t you cover us with a cloak?” Your son (Abu Dawud 587. Ahmad 5/71)"
"3475","(3475) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr ibn Salamah, who said: We were present, and the riders were passing by us. We will return from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I approached them and listened until I had memorized much of the Qur’an, and the people were With their Islam, they were waiting for the opening of Mecca. When it opened, a man came to it and said: O Messenger of God, I am the arrival of the children of so-and-so. I came to you with their Islam, so my father set out to convert his people to Islam, and when he returned, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Come forward. I have recited the Qur’an the most. So they looked while I was upon Eve, but they did not find among them anyone with more recited Qur’an than me. So they came to me while I was a boy. So I prayed with them. (Bukhari 4302. Abu Daw9 586)"
"3476","(3476) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr al-Shami, on the authority of Maasir ibn Habib, on the authority of Abu Salma ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When three Muslims go out on a journey, then let the one closest to the Book of God lead them. He was the youngest of them, so when he leads them, he is their commander, and that is the commander whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded.\n(Abdul Razzaq 9256)"
"3477","(3477) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar bin Habib Al-Jarmi, on the authority of Amr bin Salama, on the authority of his father; They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when they wanted to leave, they said: We said to him: O Messenger of God, who He prays with us? He said: Most of you collected the Qur’an, or took it from the Qur’an, but there was no one among them who collected from the Qur’an what I collected. He said: So they introduced me. And I was a boy, so I used to lead them in prayer and lead them in prayer. He said: I never witnessed a gathering of any crime except that I was their imam, and I led them in prayer. Their funerals to this day. (Abu Dawud 5888. Ahmad 5/29)"
"3478","(3478) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The people will lead in prayer, read them."
"3479","(3479) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The most learned man leads the people in prayer."
"3480","(3480) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When the immigrants came from Mecca, they camped next to Quba’, and Salim, the client of Abu Hudhayfy, led them in front of them, because he was The most prolific of them recited the Qur’an, and among them were Abu Salama bin Abdul-Asad and Omar bin Al-Khattab."
"3481","(3481) Waki’ told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar missed a man during the morning prayer, so he sent for him, Then he came and said: Where have you been? He said: I was sick, and had your messenger not come to me, I would not have gone out. So Omar said: If you are going out to Uhud, then go out to pray."
"3482","(3482) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: Whoever hears the caller, Then he did not answer it without an excuse, so there was no prayer for him."
"3483","(3483) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever heard The caller, then he did not answer without an excuse, so there was no prayer for him. (Abu Dawud 552)"
"3484","(3484) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Husayn, on the authority of Abu Najih al-Makki, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: For the ear of the son of Adam to be filled with melted lead is better for him than to hear someone calling and then not answer him."
"3485","(3485) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Whoever hears the caller does not He does not want anything good, and he does not want it."
"3486","(3486) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Hilali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, He said: Whoever hears the caller, then does not answer without an excuse, then his prayer is not valid."
"3487","(3487) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Uthman came out and had washed one side of his head. He said: The caller came and rushed to me, so I thought I would detain him."
"3488","(3488) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hayyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: There is no prayer for the neighbor of the mosque except In the mosque, he said: He was told: Who is the neighbor of the mosque? He said: Whoever is heard by the caller."
"3489","(3489) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, that he said: Whoever hears the call and does not come to it, His prayer did not go beyond his head, except with an excuse."
"3490","(3490) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: If you respond A supplication, answer the caller of God."
"3491","(3491) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled with the people in the same way. For the night in the evening prayer, meaning the dark night, he said: I had intended to command the prayer and it would be called for, then he came to a people in Their houses and I will burn them over them, so that they will not attend the prayer."
"3492","(3492) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abis, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: He came Ibn Umm Maktum went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, Medina is a land of vermin and marshland, so what about it? Is it possible for me to pray the evening and dawn prayers in my home? Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Are you listening, Hail to the prayer, Hail to the farmer? He said: He said: Yes, he said: So welcome. (Hakim 247)"
"3493","(3493) Ishaq ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, he said: Abu Razin narrated to me, on the authority of my father. Huraira, he said: Ibn Umm Maktum came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: He is a blind man whose house is vast, and he has I have a leader who follows me, so do I have a concession not to go to the mosque? Or as he said, he said: No. (Abu Dawud 553. Ahmad 3/423)"
"3494","(3494) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A wise man went to him to ask him. On the authority of a man who fasted during the day and spent the night in prayer, and neither witnessed the congregation nor the congregation, he died? He said: In Hell."
"3495","(3495) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jahm bin Abi Sabra; Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam used to have a man sitting behind him who kept his prayers."
"3496","(3496) Affan told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sirin told us, he said: Omar bin Al-Khattab was afraid Forgetting, he said: So when he prayed and appointed a man, he would look to him, and if he saw him he would stand up, and if he saw him he would sit down."
"3497","(3497) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Al-Rukān, who said: I entered upon Asma while she was praying, and she was an old man and a woman. She says to her: “Kneel down and prostrate.”"
"3498","(3498) Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad al-Darawardi told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Salma bin al-Akwa’, that he said: I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I go out and pray in one shirt? He said: Yes, and cover it even with a thorn. (Abu Dawud 632 and Ibn Khuzaymah 778)"
"3499","(3499) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, who said: I saw Salim praying with his buttons loose."
"3500","(3500) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Rabi’ ibn Sabra ibn Ma’bad al-Junni narrated to me, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the boy reaches seven years of age, command him to pray. So when he reaches ten, beat him for it. (Tirmidhi 407. Abu Dawud 495)"
"3501","(3501) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Siwar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Prophet of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Command your children to pray when they reach the age of seven, and beat them for it when they reach the age of ten, and disperse Between them in their beds. (Abu Dawud 497. Ahmad 2/180)"
"3502","(3502) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, he said: The mother of Yunus, the servant of Ibn Abbas, told me, she said: It was Ibn Abbas says: Wake the boy so he may pray even if he prostrates himself."
"3503","(3503) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of one of them, on the authority of his grandfather; Omar passed by a woman who was waking up a boy for her to pray, but he was lagging behind, so he said: Leave her alone, she is not obligated to pray. He makes her wise."
"3504","(3504) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A child is taught to pray if he knows whose right side is North"
"3505","(3505) Abu Muawiyah and Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to teach a boy to pray when he became weak."
"3506","(3506) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to teach the boys to pray when They made mistakes."
"3507","(3507) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: He used to teach his children to pray when they were of sound mind, and to fast when they were of sound mind. They could bear it."
"3508","(3508) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Hasbiy, who said: He will be commanded The boy prays when he counts twenty."
"3509","(3509) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Hasbibi’s wife, On the authority of Abd al-Rahman al-Yahsbi, similarly."
"3510","(3510) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The boy will be ordered to do it when he reaches the age of seven, and he will be beaten. upon her when he reaches ten"
"3511","(3511) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of Maimun ibn Mihran, who said: It will be commanded when he reaches His dream"
"3512","(3512) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: He used to teach a boy to pray between the ages of seven and Ten years"
"3513","(3513) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali bin Al-Hussein used to command the boys to They pray the noon and afternoon prayers together, and the sunset and evening prayers together, so it is said that they pray the prayer outside of its appointed time, so this is said. It is better than for them to sleep on it."
"3514","(3514) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A child is taught to pray if he knows his right from his left."
"3515","(3515) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, the same."
"3516","(3516) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said, “Take care of your children.” On the blessings"
"3517","(3517) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: When the boy disclosed Banu Abdul Muttalib The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, taught him this verse seven times: {Praise be to God who has not taken A son, but he has no partner in the kingdom. (Abdul Razzaq 7976)"
"3518","(3518) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali bin Al-Hussein used to teach his sons and say, “Say I believed in God and disbelieved in the tyrant."
"3519","(3519) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: They used to like to teach the boy to pray. He expresses the first thing he speaks as saying, “There is no god but Allah” seven times, so that is the first thing he speaks."
"3520","(3520) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his father, that Al-Ash’ath presented a boy, and it was said to him, and he said: I only presented the Qur’an."
"3521","(3521) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: When Al-Ash’āth came, he brought a boy, and they criticized him for that, so he said: What I presented it, but I presented the Qur’an."
"3522","(3522) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a boy to lead in prayer before he He has a wet dream during the month of Ramadan."
"3523","3523) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for the boy to lead in prayer before he He has a wet dream."
"3524","(3524) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, and Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The boy does not lead in prayer. Before he has a wet dream during the obligatory prayer or anything else."
"3525","(3525) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: A boy shall not lead the prayer until he has a wet dream."
"3526","(3526) Rawad bin Jarrah Abu Issam told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil Abi Bakr, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A boy will not lead in prayer. Until he has a wet dream."
"3527","(3527) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was disliked to stretch oneself in the presence of women, and during prayer."
"3528","(3528) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr said: Stretching takes away from the prayer."
"3529","(3529) Abu Khaled al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet forbade May God’s blessings and peace be upon him, that a man should pray in one garment, and nothing is required of him."
"3530","(3530) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he greeted; Like him\n(Muslim 277. Abu Dawud 626)"
"3531","(3531) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: The man was one of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. If he, peace and blessings of God be upon him, did not find a robe in which to pray, he placed a headband around his shoulders and then prayed."
"3532","(3532) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate exposing one’s shoulders during prayer."
"3533","(3533) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Muhammad ibn Ali used to say: A man should not pray unless he is drunk and has freed himself."
"3534","(3534) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When Umar approached Mecca, Abu He was warned and he gave the call to prayer, and said: Pray, O Commander of the Faithful, come to the prayer, come to the prayer, come to the farmer, come to the farmer. The farmer said: Woe to you, are you crazy? Was it not in your supplication that you called upon us? We will not come to you until you come to us."
"3535","(3535) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: When the people remained late, the muezzin would say: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. The prayer has begun, the prayer has begun, hail to the prayer, hail to the prayer, hail to the farmer, hail to the farmer."
"3536","(3536) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mishaj ibn Musa al-Dhabi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say to Muhammad ibn Amr: If you are in... Traveling, so I said: The sun has set, or it has not set, or the daylight has reached the middle, or it has not set, so pray before you depart."
"3537","(3537) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If you were on a journey, and you said: The sun has set or has not set, Separate"
"3538","(3538) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hamza al-Dhabi, who said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to When he arrived, he did not depart until he had prayed the noon prayer. Then Muhammad bin Amr said to him: Even if it was midday? He said: Even if it is the middle of the day. (Abu Dawud 1198. Ahmad 3/130)"
"3539","(3539) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim; He was suffering from an illness, and two men were facing each other to pray, and it was said to him: O Abu Zaid, you are here, God willing. There is an excuse, so he says: Yes, but I hear the muezzin saying: Hail to the prayer, Hail to the success, so whoever hears it, let him come to it. Even if they crawl, even if they crawl."
"3540","(3540) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman; He was being carried to the mosque when he was sick."
"3541","(3541) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I saw the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him during his illness in which he died, and he was guided between two men until he entered the row.\n(Bukhari 713)"
"3542","(3542) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Sahl, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He did not give the adhan. The muezzin thirty years ago, except when I was in the mosque."
"3543","(3543) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not give permission to leave Congregation, except for one who is afraid or sick."
"3544","(3544) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Straighten your ranks and stand close together, for I see you behind my back. Anas said: I saw one of us pressing his shoulders. With his companion's shoulder, and his foot with his foot, and if you were to go and do that, you would see one of them as if he were a mule of suns. (Bukhari 725 Ahmad 3/103)"
"3545","(3545) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he straightens the rows just as you straighten a cup. One day he saw the chest of a man coming out of the row, and he said: You will straighten your rows, or That your faces may differ from God. (Muslim 325, Abu Dawud 665)"
"3546","(3546) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Awsaja, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Straighten your ranks, so that nothing will break through you like the children of the oath. It was said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and who are the children of the deletion? He said: Black, pure sheep that will be found in the land of Yemen. (Abu Dawud 664. Ahmad 4/297)"
"3547","(3547) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Muammar, on the authority of Abu Masoud, he said: It was The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wipes our shoulders during prayer and says: “Stand straight, and do not differ lest your hearts differ.” Those of you who are versed in dreams and prohibitions will be soft among you, then those who are like you. Abu Masoud said: Today you are even more divided.\n(Muslim 122. Abu Dawud 674)"
"3548","(3548) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stand up. Your rows, for part of the goodness of prayer is to stand in row. (Bukhari 723, Muslim 124)"
"3549","(3549) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Yunus bin Jubayr, on the authority of Hattan bin Abdullah Al-Raqqashi, He said: Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari led us in prayer, and when he turned, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us and explained to us our Sunnah. He taught us our prayer, and said: When you pray, straighten your rows."
"3550","(3550) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: I was among those who evaluated Omar bin Al-Khattab. In front of him to establish the row."
"3551","(3551) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad; Omar saw something in the row, so he said with his hand like this, meaning Waki’, so he corrected it."
"3552","(3552) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Salim Abi al-Nadr, on the authority of Malik ibn Abi Amir, he said: I heard Uthman And he says: Straighten up and keep your shoulders straight, for one of the completion of the prayer is standing in a row. He said: He did not even say “Allahu Akbar.” There will come to him men whom he has appointed to establish rows."
"3553","(3553) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, and Ali’s companions said: Ali used to say: Straighten up. May your hearts be equal, and be in harmony with each other."
"3554","(3554) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwaid, on the authority of Bilal, who said: He used to straighten our shoulders and feet. In prayer"
"3555","(3555) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, he said: Abd said: God: Straighten your ranks."
"3556","(3556) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: Straighten the rows and stand close together, so that they do not separate you. The devils, as if they were the daughters of death."
"3557","(3557) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: I have not seen anyone who was more committed to the row than Omar. He would face the people in front of us, even when we said, “He said ‘Allahu Akbar.’” He would turn and look at the shoulders and feet, even if he was sending men. They expel people until they join the ranks."
"3558","(3558) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Al-Wadak, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: God laughs at three people: the people when they line up for prayer, the man who fights behind his companions, and the The man gets up in the dark of the night."
"3559","(3559) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Tamim ibn Tarfi, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Don’t you line up as the angels line up before their Lord? They said: How do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: They complete the first rows, and stand together in the row. (Muslim 1198, Abu Dawud 661)"
"3560","(3560) Shababa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Straighten your rows, and improve your bowing and prostration. (Ahmad 2/234)"
"3561","(3561) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Allaqiya, on the authority of Qutba bin Malik; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited at dawn: “And the palm trees are in plains.” (Muslim 1650, Tirmidhi 306)"
"3562","(3562) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Sari’, on the authority of Amr bin Harith; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited at dawn: {And the night when it is dark}"
"3563","(3563) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Simak, who said: I asked Jabir bin Samurah about the Prophet’s prayer, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? So he informed me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at dawn the words: {Q and the Glorious Qur’an} and the like. (Muslim 1691, Ahmad 5/105)"
"3564","(3564) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Minhal, on the authority of Abu Barzah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite it at sixty to one hundred, meaning at dawn."
"3565","(3565) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas; In the morning prayer, Abu Bakr recited Al-Baqarah, and Omar said to him when he finished: The sun would like to rise. He said: If it had risen, it would not have risen. You find us unaware."
"3566","(3566) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Khairit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf, he said: I prayed behind Omar Al-Ghadda, so he recited Yunus, Hud, and the like."
"3567","(3567) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdul-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab; Omar recited in the cave at dawn."
"3568","(3568) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir bin Rabi`, who said: I heard Omar reciting in Fajr with Surah Yusuf, slow recitation."
"3569","(3569) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Ibn Al-Farafasi told me, on the authority of his father, he said: I learned Surah Yusuf succeeded Omar in the morning."
"3570","(3570) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: Abdul led us in prayer. God Almighty dawn, so he recited two surahs, the last of which was Banu Israel."
"3571","(3571) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Idris al-Awdi, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard Ali reciting in the last part of them: {Glory be to Him. The name of your Lord}"
"3572","(3572) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubair ibn Khayrat, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I prayed. After the morning prayer, he recited Yunus and Hud."
"3573","(3573) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, who said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr speaking, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun; That Muadh bin Jabal prayed the morning prayer in Yemen and recited the Qur’an with the women, and when he came to this verse: {And God took Abraham as a friend} he said A man behind him: Umm Ibrahim’s eyes were refreshed."
"3574","(3574) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to recite the surah that Joseph is mentioned therein, and Al-Kahf is mentioned therein."
"3575","(3575) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, who said: Our imam used to recite by us At dawn with the surah from the Meen."
"3576","(3576) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man ibn Qays, on the authority of Ubaidah; He used to recite “Al-Rahman” and the like at dawn."
"3577","(3577) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I prayed behind Arfaja, and perhaps he recited at the tables at dawn."
"3578","(3578) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Idris’ grandfather, who said: I prayed behind Ali in the morning, so he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}"
"3579","(3579) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Anbari’s repentance; He heard Abu Siwar al-Qadi say: I prayed behind Ibn al-Zubayr in the morning, and I heard him reciting: {Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with Aad? Iram of the pillar}"
"3580","(3580) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, who said: I prayed behind Abraham, and he used to recite in the morning: (Yas) and the like, and he was quick to read."
"3581","(3581) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He said: I have never seen a man recite more than Ali. Indeed, he recited for us in the dawn prayer with the prophets. He said: When he reached the head of He left out seventy verses and recited what came after them, then he mentioned them and came back and recited them, then he returned to the place where he had recited. When it stutters"
"3582","(3582) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Dahhak ibn Uthman informed us, saying: I saw Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz reciting at dawn. With two surahs from the length of the chapter."
"3583","(3583) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, who said: Omar used to recite in prayer. Fajr prayer with a hundred from the cows, and it is followed by a surah from the two verses, or from the beginnings of the chapter, and it is recited with a hundred from Al Imran, He follows it with a surah from the two surahs, or from the surah al-mufassil."
"3584","(3584) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Husayn bin Sabri, who said: I prayed behind Omar, In the first rak'ah he recited Surah Yusuf, then in the second he recited with the star, prostrated, then he got up and recited: {When the earth shook} then He bowed down"
"3585","(3585) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: I heard Omar sobbing. \nI was at the last of the rows in the morning prayer and he was reciting: {I only complain of my grief and my sorrow to God}"
"3586","(3586) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Waqqas, he said: I heard Omar; Then he mentioned something similar to it."
"3587","(3587) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Hamza al-A’war, on the authority of Ibrahim; He led them in prayer with them on the Friday of Fajr, so he recited with: (کیعص)۔"
"3588","(3588) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Bishr al-Hajimi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: We were contemplating the resurrection of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon and afternoon. The dhahur in the first two rak’ahs was as much as thirty verses, and we estimated his standing in the other two rak’ahs to be half. From that, we predicted his resurrection in the first two rak’ahs of the afternoon as much as the other two rak’ahs of the afternoon, and we predicted His resurrection in the other two days of the afternoon was half of that. (Abu Dawud 8000, Ahmad 3/2)"
"3589","(3589) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} and in the morning for a longer period of time than That \n(Muslim 338. Ahmad 5/86)"
"3590","(3590) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite at noon and afternoon: {the heavens and the one who shines}, and {and the heavens with signs}.\n(Tayalisi 774, Ibn Hibban 1827)"
"3591","(3591) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: Hisham Al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite for us in the first two rak’ahs of At noon, he would lengthen the first part of the prayer and shorten the second part, and he would do that during the morning prayer, making the first part long. He shortened the second rak'ah, and he used to recite for us in the two rak'ahs of the afternoon prayer. (Bukhari 759. Muslim 333)"
"3592","(3592) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, guessed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, reciting it at noon is similar to (Al-Am Revealing)."
"3593","(3593) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jad’an, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: I heard a melody from Omar. From (Q) in the noon prayer."
"3594","(3594) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Mutawakkil Al-Naji; Omar recited in the back: {Q}, {and the offspring}"
"3595","(3595) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I prayed behind Anas al-Dhahr, and he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, And He made us hear the verses."
"3596","(3596) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Jamil ibn Murā, on the authority of Muwarriq al-Ijali, who said: I prayed behind Ibn Umar. At noon, he recited Surah Maryam."
"3597","(3597) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Saif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr reciting in the dhahr: {"
"3598","(3598) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Indeed, I recite at noon with: {Al-Saffat}"
"3599","(3599) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, he said: Reciting at noon and dawn is the same."
"3600","(3600) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The noon prayer is equated with dawn."
"3601","(3601) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Uqba ibn Nafi’, who said: I heard Ibn Umar whispering about the Qur’āt in Dhuhr and Asr."
"3602","(3602) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer, and when he gave the salutation, he said: Has any of you recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}? Then a man from the people said: “I am.” He said: “I learned that some of you have entered it.” (Muslim 2998, Abu Dawud 825)"
"3603","(3603) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar and Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Asr and Maghrib Either way"
"3604","(3604) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The zahir is multiplied by four times. Bitterness"
"3605","(3605) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to equate the afternoon prayer with dinner, And the afternoon prayer in Morocco."
"3606","(3606) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Samak bin Harb, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon and afternoon: {the heavens and the one who sets out}, {and the heavens with signs}."
"3607","(3607) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to equate the rak’ahs of the noon and the afternoon prayers."
"3608","(3608) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Abu al-Rabi’, on the authority of Abu al-Aaliyah, he said: The afternoon On half of the back."
"3609","(3609) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The word “Al-Tur” is recited in the Maghrib prayer. (Bukhari 8651 Muslim 174)"
"3610","(3610) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his mother; Indeed, she heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting in Morocco: {And the Mursalat}. (Bukhari 7631, Muslim 338)"
"3611","(3611) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zaid, or Abu Ayyub; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in Maghrib the Al-A’raf in all two rak’ahs. (Bukhari 864. Ahmad 5/185)"
"3612","(3612) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in Morocco: “The fig and the olive.” (Tahawi 214)"
"3613","(۳۶۱۳) حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو الأَحْوَصِِ ، عَنْ أَبِی إِسْحَاقَ ، عَنْ عَمْرِو بْنِ مَیْمُونٍ ، قَالَ : صَلَّی بِنَا عُمَرُ صَلاَۃَ الْمَغْرِبِ ، فَقَرَأَ In the first rak'ah it says: {The figs and olives}, and in the second rak'ah: {Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the companions of the elephant}, and {For the people of Quraysh}۔"
"3614","(3614) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, who said: Abu Musa read to me the letter of Omar: Recite to the people in Morocco at the end of Al-Mufassal."
"3615","(3615) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of al-Nazzal bin Ammar, he said: Abu Uthman al-Nahdi told me, he said: Abu Masoud led us in the Maghrib prayer and recited: (Say, “He is God, One”), and I wished that he had recited Surah Al-Baqarah, with goodness. His voice"
"3616","(3616) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abdullah bin [corrupt]Laharith; Ibn Abbas read Al-Dukhan in Morocco."
"3617","(3617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Nawfal ibn Abi Aqrab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I heard it. It is recited in Morocco {When God's victory and conquest come}."
"3618","(3618) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Ibn Umar reciting: (Q) in Morocco."
"3619","(3619) Abdă narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar once recited in Morocco the following verse: (Yās"
"3620","(3620) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; It was recited in Morocco with: (Yasin) and (am yatasalaun)."
"3621","(3621) Husayn bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Imran bin Husayn used to recite In Morocco {when the earth shakes} and (Al-Adiyat)."
"3622","(3622) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr reciting in Morocco. Sometimes {telling her news} and sometimes {telling her news}"
"3623","(3623) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhallāl, who said: I heard Ibrahim reciting in the first rak’ah of the Maghrib prayer. Quraysh}"
"3624","(3624) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, he said: Al-Hasan used to recite in the Maghrib: (When I am shaken) (and the ordinary ones) no. He called her."
"3625","(3625) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: Umm Muadh A group of people were praying the Maghrib prayer, then a boy from the Ansar passed by them while he was working on his camel, so Muadh stayed with them for a long time, and when he saw That boy left the prayer and set off in search of his camel, so that matter was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Infatuation. Are you, Moaz? Doesn't one of you recite in Morocco: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} and {The sun in its brightness}"
"3626","(3626) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Nasir bin Dhuluq, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim; He used to recite in Morocco in short, detailed verses: {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"3627","(3627) Yazid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Othman, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz reciting in Morocco. Briefly detailed."
"3628","(3628) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, it is recited in the evening prayer: “And the figs and the olives” (Bukhari 7671, Muslim 175)"
"3629","(3629) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Abdullah led us in the evening prayer. The last, so he opened the nostrils until he reached: {So know that God is your Protector. He is the best Protector and the best Helper} He bowed down, then he got up and recited the verse. The second is with a surah."
"3630","(3630) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah; Like him"
"3631","(3631) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, who said: Abu Musa read to me the letter of Omar. To him: To recite to the people at dinner in the middle of the joint."
"3632","(3632) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Masruq bin Al-Ajda’; Othman recited during the night prayer, meaning “the star,” then he prostrated, then he got up and recited “the figs and the olives.”"
"3633","(3633) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Abbad, he said: Hilal narrated to me; He heard Abu Hurairah reciting {and the ordinary women are slaughtered} in the evening prayer."
"3634","(3634) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Omar used to recite in Al-Isha’ the words “those who disbelieved” and “Al-Fath”."
"3635","(3635) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to recite in the evening prayers “the revelation of” the prostration, and he would bow with it."
"3636","(3636) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjouf, he said: Abu Rafi’ narrated to us, he said: I prayed Isha’ with Omar. So he recited: {When the heavens split open}"
"3637","(3637) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Othman informed me, he said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz reciting in Dinner in the middle of the joint."
"3638","(3638) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit. With the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He said: There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book. (Bukhari 756 and Abu Dawud 818)"
"3639","(3639) Ismail Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub; Abu Al-Sa'ib told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays A prayer that was not recited with the opening of the book, so it is prematurity, prematurity, incomplete prematurity. (Muslim 2968, Abu Dawud 817)"
"3640","(3640) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Every prayer is not recited. With the opening of the Book, it is Khadaj."
"3641","(3641) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Abi Hisham, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, he said: Jabir ibn Abd said: God: Whoever does not recite in every rak’ah the Umm al-Qur’an does not pray, except behind the imam."
"3642","(3642) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Imran Ibn Husayn, who said: No. It is permissible to perform a prayer in which the opening of the book is not recited and the two verses are recited onwards."
"3643","(3643) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadrah, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; In every prayer there is a recitation of the Qur’an, the Mother of the Book, or more."
"3644","(3444) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Ubayah bin Rabi’i, who said: Omar said: It is not sufficient. A prayer in which it is not recited with the opening of the book and two verses onwards."
"3645","(3645) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: I sat with a group of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. Among the Ansar, they mentioned prayer and said: There is no prayer except with a recitation of it, even with the Mother of the Book. Khaled said: So I said To Abdullah bin Al-Harith: Will you name any of them? He said: Yes, Khawat bin Jubayr."
"3646","(3646) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the opening of the book is not recited in every rak’ah He will repeat that rak’ah."
"3647","(3447) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Hakam; Abu Wa'il recited the opening of the Book and its verses, then bowed."
"3648","(3648) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The conqueror is sufficient. The letter. He said: I met it after that, and I said: About the obligatory prayer? He said: Yes."
"3649","(3649) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The opener of the Book is sufficient in the obligatory prayer. And others."
"3650","(3650) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Baraa’, who said: I said to Ibn Umar: Is it necessary to perform every rak’ah? Do I read? He said: I am ashamed before the Lord of this House not to recite in every rak’ah the opening of the Book, and whatever is possible. And she asked Ibn Abbas? He said: He is your imam, so if you wish, then less of him, and if you wish, then more of him."
"3651","(3651) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Yahya, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; He recited: {two prayers}, then he bowed."
"3652","(3652) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan Al-Saadi, on the authority of Abu Nadhra, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: There is no prayer for the one who does not recite in every rak’ah: (Praise be to God) and an obligatory surah. And others.\n(Tirmidhi 238 and Ibn Majah 839)"
"3653","(3653) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We were talking, that there is no prayer except With your reading, he opened the Book and nothing more."
"3654","(3654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The opener of the Book is sufficient for voluntary prayer."
"3655","(3655) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Muammar, he said: We said: To Khabab: How do you know the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon and afternoon? He said: Because of the disorder in his beard, and Abu Muawiyah said: Because of his beard. (Bukhari 777. Abu Dawud 797)"
"3656","(3656) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Za’ara’, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of the one who heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: “They knew how to recite it at noon and afternoon with the disturbance of their beard.” (Ahmad 5/371)"
"3657","(3657) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: What Do you know, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon and afternoon prayers? But we read. (Abu Dawud 8051. Ahmad 1/249)"
"3658","(3658) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Habib ibn Shahid, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: In every prayer I read, for what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, declared, we made known, and what he concealed, we concealed. (Bukhari 772, Muslim 44)"
"3659","(3659) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, he said: Khabab bin Al-Art He recites the recitation aloud at noon and afternoon prayers."
"3660","(3660) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Kilab ibn Amr, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I learned {when the earth shook} behind Khabbab in the afternoon."
"3661","(3661) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Sa`id bin Al-Aas led the people in the noon or afternoon prayer, so he recited the recitation out loud, and the people glorified God, so he continued to recite it, and when he finished He ascended the pulpit and addressed the people, saying: In every prayer there is a recitation, and the daytime prayer silences people, and I hated to be silent, so do not You see that I did that out of heresy."
"3662","(3662) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muzahim, who said: I prayed behind Sa’id bin Jubayr, The first class was the one who understood its recitation at noon and afternoon prayers."
"3663","(3663) Hammad bin Masadhi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I prayed behind Anas during the noon prayer, and he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} And He made us hear the verses."
"3664","(3644) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali Ibn Zayd Ibn Jud’an, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: I heard from Omar Naghma from (Q) At noon"
"3665","(3665) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; Al-Aswad and Al-Qamah used to prostrate in prayer at noon and afternoon, so they did not prostrate."
"3666","(3666) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, Salim, Al-Qasim, and Mujahid, And giving; About a man who pronounces the loud voice at noon or afternoon? They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"3667","(3667) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Bashir, on the authority of his leaders; A man spoke out loud at noon and afternoon prayers, but he did not prostrate."
"3668","(3668) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who speaks loudly in something in which he does not speak loudly? He said: He prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"3669","(3669) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he speaks loudly about what he or she is afraid of, he or she is afraid. When he recites it out loud, he performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"3670","(3670) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, saying: Laith narrated to us, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Whoever misses any part of the imam’s prayer, then if he wishes He speaks out loud, and if he wishes, he does not speak out loud."
"3671","(3671) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: Do like what the Imam did."
"3672","(3672) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Hakim, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz Like it"
"3673","(3673) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Ubaid bin Umair went to Raka’i from Morocco, and I heard him reciting. : {And the night when it covers}"
"3674","(3674) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Mufaddal ibn Mihalil, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to find it desirable for those who He preceded some of the prayers at dawn, sunset, or evening prayer when he stood up to make up for it, to recite the recitation out loud, as he knew. Who does not know that recitation is in what is decreed?"
"3675","(3675) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prays Maghrib alone, he said: His ears hear its recitation."
"3676","(3676) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Najih, who said: I was with Sa’id bin Jubayr, so we went to Maghrib and we had already performed a rak'ah, so when Sa'id stood up and performed it, he recited: {Your deity is multiplication}"
"3677","(3677) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Ubaidah; In the recitation during the daytime prayer, listen to yourself."
"3678","(3678) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah (h) and on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ibn Sabit, They said: The minimum for the Qur’an to be recited is for your ears to hear it."
"3679","(3679) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: I prayed next to Abdullah By daylight, I did not know what he recited, until he ended with his saying: {My Lord, increase me in knowledge}, so I thought he was reciting it. Taha"
"3680","(3680) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He narrated to me someone who prayed behind Ibn Masoud, and he mentioned something similar to the hadith Wakee'"
"3681","(3681) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw a man reciting the recitation out loud during the day, so he called him and said: The daytime prayer is not recited out loud, so explain your recitation."
"3682","(3682) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: Ibn Sirin used to volunteer, and we used to listen to his recitation, so when he stood up for prayer. What is read is hidden from us."
"3683","(3683) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad used to volunteer during the day and listen."
"3684","(3684) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The daytime prayer is strange, and the night prayer is easy for your ears to hear."
"3685","(3685) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, who said: A man prayed next to Abu Ubaidah and he recited the Qur’an recitation out loud, so he said: To him: The daytime prayer is strange, and the night prayer is easy for your ears to hear."
"3686","(3686) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in him blazing through the Fire. Voluntary if it does not harm anyone."
"3687","(3687) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: I stood next to Abdullah while he was praying. In the mosque, I did not know that it was being recited until I heard him say: {My Lord, increase me in knowledge}, then I knew that it was being recited in a surah. Taha"
"3688","(3688) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun; Omar bin Abdul Aziz prayed and raised his voice, so Saeed sent to him: What are you, oh man?"
"3689","(3689) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: They said: O Messenger of God, indeed Are we a people who dare to recite the Qur’an by fire? He said: Throw them into the sand. (Tabarani 3896)"
"3690","(3690) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Asim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: So You read, so let your ears listen, for the heart is equal between the tongue and the ear."
"3691","(3691) Mukhlid bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Hakim bin Aqal; He forbade raising the voice when reciting recitation during the day, and said: He may raise it at night if he wishes."
"3692","(3692) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Yahya bin Ja’dah, on the authority of Umm Hani’, she said: I used to listen to the recitation of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while I was on my throne. (Tirmidhi 318, Ahmad 6/341)"
"3693","(3693) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: They said to him: How were Abd’s reciters? God by night? He said: Sometimes he used to hear the family of Utbah. He said: They were in his room between his hands, and his scholars were among those who He paid it."
"3694","(3694) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: He spent the night with Abdullah, on the authority of Laila. They said to him: How was your recitation? He said: He used to listen to the people of the house."
"3695","(3695) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, he said: It was When a man recites, he announces his recitation, then Muadh stopped him and said: Where is the one who used to awaken the teeth? And he rebukes, or expels, Satan."
"3696","(3696) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr, who said: Omar spent the night with us. So I stood up praying and hid my voice. She said: Don’t you recite your recitation out loud? The only thing that woke us up was the voice of Muadh Al-Qari, and Abu Ayyub’s servant succeeded."
"3697","(3697) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurriyah, on the authority of al-Hasan; He used to pray at night, and the people of his house would hear him."
"3698","(3698) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: The night prayer, let your ears hear."
"3699","(3699) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: I prayed with Abdullah one night All of them, and he would raise his voice, recite the Qur’an so that the people of the mosque could hear it, and would recite without stopping."
"3700","(3700) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, and Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, he said: He said: Abdullah: Whoever hears his ears does not fear."
"3701","(3701) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Zayed bin Nushit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbiy, on the authority of his father Huraira, he said: When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would get up during the night, he would lower one stage and raise one stage. \n(Abu Dawud 1322 and Ibn Hibban 2603)"
"3702","(3702) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Ma’ar bin Suwayd, who said: We went out with Omar as pilgrims, so he prayed. We brought the dawn, so it was recited with: (Have you not seen) and (to ilāf)"
"3703","(3703) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jami’ al-Muharbibi, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, who said: Omar led us in prayer. At dawn during travel, it was recited with: {Say, O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is God, One}."
"3704","(3704) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They recite short surahs on the journey."
"3705","(3705) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I went out with Anas, and he used to recite for us at dawn: {Glorify the Name Your Lord is the Most High} and the like."
"3706","(3706) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, he said: Ibn Masoud led us in prayer. At dawn on the journey, he recited to the last of the Children of Israel: {Praise be to God who has not taken a son} then he bowed."
"3707","(3707) Ali bin Ubaid told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Al-Jaad, he said: I was with Ibn Umar on a journey, and he led the dawn prayer with us, reciting to us: {When the sun was rounded}"
"3708","(3708) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin al-Ghaz, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir al-Jhani, who said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and when dawn came he called the call to prayer and performed the iqama, then he made me remain on his right, then he recited With the two exorcists. When he left, he said: How did you see? I said: I have seen, O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So recite them whenever you sleep and as you get up. (Abu Dawud 1457. Ahmad 4/144)"
"3709","(3709) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to recite ten surahs, more and less, in the rak'ah."
"3710","(3710) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, Na’ilah Ibn al-Farafsiyah said: Al-Kalbiyya, where they entered upon Othman and killed him. She said: Whether you kill him or call him, he was alive during the night. A prayer in which the Qur’an is collected."
"3711","(3711) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Tamim al-Dari used to recite the entire Qur’an in one rak’ah."
"3712","(3712) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Indeed, I recite the surah from the detailed one in two rak’ahs."
"3713","(3713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Abi Ishaq, he said: Bakr bin Ma’iz told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym; It is recited with the two and three surahs in the rak’ah."
"3714","(3714) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to combine the two surahs in one rak'ah of the obligatory prayer."
"3715","(3715) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’; What about a man who prays the obligatory prayer and recites two surahs in one rak’ah, or one surah in two rak’ahs? He said: No problem."
"3716","(3716) Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; What about a man who combines the two surahs in one rak’ah? He said: As for the verses of the verse “Mi’in”, kneel with every surah, and as for the verses of “Mathani” and “Mufassal”, recite if you wish."
"3717","(3717) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafali; He used to recite the two surahs in rak'ah."
"3718","(3718) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salim, who said: Relate as many times as you wish."
"3719","(3719) Ali bin Hashim and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed seven long rak’ahs, except that he stood still. He said: He recited."
"3720","(3720) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Uthman, He said: I stood behind the shrine and prayed, and I wanted no one to overpower me that night. He said: Then a man He winked at me from behind me, and I did not turn around. Then he winked at me and I turned around, and behold, Othman bin Affan. I stepped aside and he came forward, and he recited the Qur’an. In one rak'ah, then he left."
"3721","(3721) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Waqa’i, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr combining two surahs. In every rak'ah of the obligatory prayer."
"3722","(3722) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Kammis narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq al-Uqaili, who said: I said to Aisha: It was Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, combine the two surahs in one rak’ah? She said: Yes, Al-Mufassal.\n(Abu Dawud 1286. Ahmad 6/218)"
"3723","(3723) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He used to recite at dawn in the first rak’ah with: (Ham) the smoke, (Al-Tur), and the jinn, and he would recite in the second with the last. Al-Baqarah and the last of the family of Imran, and with the short surah."
"3724","(3724) Ibn Numayr and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Mustarid bin Al-Ahnaf, On the authority of Sala, on the authority of Hudhayfy, he said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he opened the cows, and I said: He should seal them. He kneels with it, then he opened the family of Imran, and I said: He seals it and kneels with it, then he opened an-Nisa’, and I said: He kneels with it. So he recited until he concluded it."
"3725","(3725) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muammar ibn Musa, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: Two surahs should not be combined in every verse. Rakaa"
"3726","(3726) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, who said: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman bin al-Harith bin Hisham does not combine two surahs in a rak’ah, nor does he skip a surah if he ends them, even He kneels."
"3727","(3727) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman; He did not combine two surahs in a rak'ah."
"3728","(3728) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zayd ibn Khalid Al-Janni, who said: I do not like Indeed, I recited two surahs in my rak’ah, even if I had red camels."
"3729","(3729) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zaid bin Khalid; Like him"
"3730","(3730) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: He who heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrated to me. He says: Give each surah its share of bowing and prostration. (Bayhaqi 10. Ahmad 5/59)"
"3731","(3731) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Israel narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Give each A Surah that protects you from bowing and prostration."
"3732","(3732) Abdă and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, or Zayd ibn Thabit; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the Al-A’raf in two rak’ahs in Maghrib."
"3733","(3733) Abdah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Abu Bakr recited Al-A’raf in two rak’ahs in Morocco."
"3734","(3734) Abdă and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Abu Bakr recited Al-Baqarah in two rak’ahs at dawn."
"3735","(3735) Abdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib; Omar recited Bālī Imran in the first two rak’ahs of Isha’, which he interrupted, meaning in both of them."
"3736","(3736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Omar bin Ya’la, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to recite at dawn with the children of Israel in the two rak'ahs."
"3737","(3737) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer behind Sa’id ibn Jubayr, so he recited with: (Ham) the believer. When he reached (evening and early) he bowed, then he got up the second time and recited the rest of the surah, then he bowed, and did not You have Qunoot."
"3738","(3738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, who said: He used to recite the surah in the two rak’ahs of dawn."
"3739","(3739) Abduh told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to divide the surah into two rak'ahs."
"3740","(3740) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is no harm in dividing the surah into two rak’ahs."
"3741","(3741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yahya, who said: A surah is divided in the two rak’ahs of Fajr."
"3742","(3742) Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in dividing the surah into two rak’ahs."
"3743","(3743) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Ibn Masoud used to recite At noon and afternoon, in the first two rak'ahs, with the opening of the book, and whatever is possible, and in the last two rak'ahs with the opening The book"
"3744","(3744) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar wrote to Shurayh, reciting in The first two are the opening of the Book and a surah, and the last two are the opening of the Book."
"3745","(3745) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ibrahim Ibn Al-Harith said: I heard Hisham Ibn Ismail on the pulpit of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: It was Abu Al-Darda’ says: In the first two rak’ahs of the Dhuhr prayer, recite the Umm al-Kitab and a surah, and in the last two rak’ahs With Fatiha The Book, and in the last rak’ah of Maghrib with Umm al-Kitab, and in the two rak’ahs of Isha’ with Umm al-Kitab."
"3746","(3746) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: It was narrated Abu Al-Darda’ used to say: In the first two rak’ahs of the noon and afternoon prayers, recite the opening of the Book and its surahs, and in The last two rak’ahs of the Maghrib prayer, and in the last two rak’ahs of the evening prayer. With the Mother of the Book"
"3747","(3747) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of his uncle, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Rafi’, on the authority of Ali; He used to say: The imam and those behind him recite at noon and afternoon in the first two rak’ahs the opening of the book. And a surah, and in the other two it is the opening of the book."
"3748","(3748) Abdullah bin Mubarak and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’ bin Hawwa, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Sanabihi, who said: I prayed with Abu Bakr at sunset, so I came close to him until my clothes touched his clothes, or The end of his garment. Ibn Mubarak doubted, so he recited in the third rak’ah with the opening of the Book, and said: {Our Lord, do not let our hearts deviate after When You guided us}"
"3749","(3749) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is recited in the first two rak’ahs. With the opening of the book and a surah, and in the other two with the opening of the book, we used to say that there is no prayer except with the recitation of the opening of the book. The book and what it adds."
"3750","(3750) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Malik; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite at noon and afternoon prayers in all of them. (Tabarani 2437)"
"3751","(3751) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to recite in the four rak’ahs, making it equal. between us"
"3752","(3752) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, he said: Omar bin Abi Suhaim narrated to me, he said: It was Abdullah bin Mughaffal ordered the prayer in which the imam does not force himself to recite during the prayer in the two rak’ahs The first two are the opening of the Book and a surah, and the last two are the opening of the Book."
"3753","(3753) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to say: Recite in the first two verses with the Fatihah. The Book and its Surahs, and in the Hereafter with the Opener of the Book."
"3754","(3754) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Read in The last two are the opening of the book."
"3755","3755) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah and Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h) and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hassan, they said: Recite in the two rak’ahs, meaning the other two, at noon and afternoon, with the opening of the book."
"3756","(3756) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he does not recite in one rak’ah with the opening of the book, He performs that rak'ah."
"3757","(3757) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha; In the daytime prayer, in the first two rak’ahs, she used to recite the opening of the Book and a surah, and in the last two rak’ahs With the opening of the Book."
"3758","(3758) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Recite the Fatihah in the first two rak’ahs. The Book and a Surah, and in the other two it is the opening of the Book."
"3759","(3759) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Humaid bin Salman, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard him reciting in the other two Dhuhr and Asr with the Opener of the Book."
"3760","(3760) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Salama bin Nubait, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Like him"
"3761","(3761) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Read in all of them."
"3762","(3762) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammam, and Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the first two rak’ahs the opening of the Book and a surah, and in The last two are the opening of the book. (Bukhari 776 and Abu Dawud 795)"
"3763","(3763) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, that they said: Recite in the first two verses, and glorify God. In the other two."
"3764","(3764) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He said: He recites in the first two, and says “Tasbih” in the last two."
"3765","(3765) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Ibrahim: What should be done in the other two rak’ahs of the prayer? He said: Glory be to God, praise be to God, and God is great."
"3766","(3766) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Glory be to God in the last two and God is great."
"3767","(3767) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, who said: The Fatihah is recited in the first two rak’ahs. The Qur’an and a surah, and in the other two he glorifies and exalts Him."
"3768","(3768) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He glorifies and glorifies in The other two are praising Him."
"3769","(3769) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Jawab bin Ubaid Allah al-Taymi, he said: Yazid told us Ibn Sharik Al-Taymi, Abu Ibrahim, said: I asked Omar Ibn Al-Khattab about reciting prayers behind the imam? So he said to me: Read. I said: Even if I were behind you? He said: Even if you are behind me. I said: Even if you read? He said: Even if you read."
"3770","(3770) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas It is read behind the imam in the Dhuhr prayer from Surat Maryam."
"3771","(3771) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I prayed next to Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba. He said: I heard him reciting behind the imam. He said: I met Mujahid and mentioned that to him. He said: Mujahid said: I heard Abdullah bin Amr recites behind the imam."
"3772","(3772) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Tharwan, on the authority of Dhudhail, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud; In the afternoon prayer, behind the imam, in the two rak'ahs, he recited the Fatihah of the Book and a surah."
"3773","(3773) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Sulaym, on the authority of Abu Maryam Al-Asadi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: I prayed to Next to him, I heard him reciting behind some of the princes at noon and afternoon."
"3774","(3774) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi’; That Ali used to say: Recite at noon and afternoon behind the imam in every rak’ah with the Umm al-Kitab and a surah."
"3775","(3775) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; That Ali used to order the recitation to be recited behind the imam."
"3776","(3776) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not neglect to recite the opening of the book behind the imam. He spoke out loud, or he did not speak out."
"3777","(3777) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ubadah bin The silent one, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the evening prayer with us, but the recitation became difficult for him, so when he left, he said: Perhaps you will recite behind your imam? He said: We said: Yes, O Messenger of God, we will do it. He said: Do not do it except by the Mother of the Qur’an, for there is no prayer except by her."
"3778","(3778) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Qalab; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to his companions: Do you recite behind your imam? Some said: Yes, and some said: No, so he said: If you must do it, then let one of you recite the book and discover it within yourself."
"3779","(3779) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abi Qalabi, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Similar to the hadith of Hashim.\n(Ahmad 4/236; Abd al-Razzaq 2766)"
"3780","(3780) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Al-Fayd, who said: I heard Abu Shaybah Al-Mahri speaking, on the authority of Muadh ; He said: Concerning a man praying behind the imam: If he hears his recitation, he recites: {Say: He is God, One}, and {Say, I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind}, and {Say I seek refuge in the Lord of Creation} His people said: or something similar, and if he does not hear the recitation, then let him read, and do not harm anyone who To his right, and to his left."
"3781","(3781) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: You have the choice. If you want, then recite, and if you want, then keep the habit."
"3782","(3782) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If the reciting people do not listen to the imam, then recite Within yourself if you wish."
"3783","(3783) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour and Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: Read behind the imam in every rak’ah with the opening of the book in your heart."
"3784","(3784) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Shaybani told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He used to say: Read behind the imam at noon and afternoon with the opening of the book and a surah, and in the other two with the opening of it. The book"
"3785","(3785) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail bin Salem told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say: The Qara’i are behind The imam at noon and afternoon is a light for prayer."
"3786","(3786) Abbad told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He said: The imam and those behind him recite at noon and afternoon the opening of the book."
"3787","(3787) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, who said: Recite behind the imam when he does not pronounce, in The first two are the opening of the Book and a surah, and the last two are the opening of the Book."
"3788","(3788) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: Be silent about what is spoken, and recite what is not spoken. He speaks out loud"
"3789","(3789) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I prayed the sunset prayer while Al-Hakam bin Ayyub was our imam. Abu Malih was next to Ibn Usama, and I heard him reciting with the opening of the book. When the imam greeted, I said to Abu Malih: Read. Behind the imam while he is reading? He said: Did you hear something? I said: Yes, he said: Yes."
"3790","(3790) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Tha’labah, on the authority of Anas; He said in the recitation of the Qur’an behind the imam, “Tasbih.”"
"3791","(3791) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Raja’ ibn Hiyaw, on the authority of Mahmoud ibn Rabi’, who said: I prayed a prayer. And next to me was Ubadah ibn al-Samit. He said: So he recited the opening of the book. He said: So I said to him: O Abu al-Walid, did I not hear you? Do you recite with the opening of the book? He said: Yes, there is no prayer except with it."
"3792","(3792) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If you read behind[corrupt] The imam is good, but if you do not recite, it is sufficient for you to recite the imam."
"3793","(3793) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Harith Al-Abdi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Read behind the imam with the opening of the book."
"3794","(3794) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Sha’abi improving his recitation behind the imam."
"3795","(3795) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of My father said: I do not like to occupy myself during the noon and afternoon prayers behind the imam."
"3796","(3796) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya’qub, that Abu al-Sa’ib He told him, he said: I said to Abu Hurairah: Should I be behind the imam? He touched my arm and said: O Persian, recite it to yourself. He means the Mother of the Qur’an."
"3797","(3797) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Ukaymah, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: Pray. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. We think it was the morning prayer. When he finished it, he said: Has any of you recited? A man said: I am. He said: I say: Why should I dispute the Qur’an? (Tirmidhi 312. Ahmad 2/284)"
"3798","(3798) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Imran bin hippocampus; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the noon prayer, and when he gave the salutation, he said: Has any of you recited “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High”? Then a man from the people said: “I am.” He said: “I learned that some of you have entered it.”"
"3799","(3799) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, He said: We were reciting behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You have confused the Qur’an with me. \n(Ahmad 1/451, Abu Ali 4985)"
"3800","(3800) Sharik and Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever has an imam, he will have reciters."
"3801","(3801) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: A man came to Abdullah and said: Should I recite behind the imam? Then Abdullah said to him: There is work in prayer, and that imam will suffice for you."
"3802","(3802) Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Asbaani told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Asbaani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ali, He said: Whoever recites behind the imam has committed a natural mistake."
"3803","(3803) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Dawud ibn Qais, on the authority of Abu Bijad, on the authority of Sa`d, he said: I wish that the It is recited behind the imam: There is a Jamaraat in it."
"3804","(3804) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata bin Yassar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: There is no reciting behind the imam."
"3805","(3805) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, and Anas ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar said: It is enough for you to recite it. Imam"
"3806","(3806) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, and Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He said Al-Aswad: Because I bite on a hot coal, it is more beloved to me than reciting behind an imam whom I know is reciting."
"3807","(3807) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Maqsim, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Do not recite behind the imam."
"3808","(3808) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Uthman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Thawban, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit said: Do not recite behind the imam if he is loud, nor if he is silent."
"3809","(3809) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Musa ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: Whoever recites behind the imam, do not May peace be upon him."
"3810","(3810) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled informed us, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, He said: I wish that the one who recites behind the imam would have his mouth filled with dust."
"3811","(3811) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, the same."
"3812","(3812) Mu’ammar narrated to us, Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, he said: I asked Abu Sa’id about the Qur’an reciters behind the imam? He said: That imam is sufficient for you."
"3813","(3813) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I asked him about reciting prayers behind the imam? He said: There are no reciters behind the imam."
"3814","(3814) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Listen to the imam."
"3815","(3815) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I do not know of the Sunni Qara’i behind the imam."
"3816","(3816) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated reciting behind the imam, and he used to say: It is sufficient for you to recite behind the imam."
"3817","(3817) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Qays, who said: I asked Suwayd ibn Ghafli: Should I recite behind the imam in Noon and afternoon? He said: No."
"3818","(3818) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Kibran, who said: Al-Dahhak used to forbid reciting behind the imam."
"3819","(3819) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Malik ibn Ammarah, who said: I asked, I do not know, how many men from The companions of Abdullah all say: It should not be recited behind an imam. Among them is Amr bin Maimun."
"3820","(3820) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The imam has only been appointed to be followed, so when he says “Allahu Akbar,” then “Allahu Akbar.” And when he recites, listen carefully.\n(Abu Dawud 604, Ahmad 2/376)"
"3821","(3821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ukil, on the authority of Ibrahim He said: The one who recites behind the imam is difficult."
"3822","(3822) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: It is sufficient for you. Imam’s reciter."
"3823","(3823) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Everyone who has an imam, his reciters will have his reciters."
"3824","(3824) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awsaja, on the authority of al-Bara’ ibn Azib, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God and His angels pray over the first row.\n(Abu Dawud 664, Ahmad 4/684)"
"3825","(3825) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Awsaja, On the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: God and His angels send blessings upon the first rows.\n(Ahmad 4/299, Ibn Khuzaymah 1552)"
"3826","(3826) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of al-Bara’ ibn Aazib, who said: God And His angels pray on the front row."
"3827","(3827) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It was said: The best ranks of men are the front ones. The worst of women's rows is their front."
"3828","(3828) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dirar, on the authority of Zazan, who said: If the people knew what is in the front row, they would not be able to estimate it. upon him except by lottery."
"3829","(3829) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: It used to be said: Indeed, God and His angels send blessings upon him. Those who pray in the first rows."
"3830","(3830) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind narrated to us, saying: It was narrated that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: O Messenger of God, guide me to a job that I can do. He said: Be the imam of your people. He said: What if I cannot? He said: Be their muezzin. He said: What if I am not able? He said: So be in the first row. (Bukhari 59)"
"3831","(3831) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I was with Abdullah bin Shaddad, and I performed the prayer. He said: So he made He says: They advanced, they advanced, for it was said: God and His angels bless those who pray in the front rows. (Abdul Razzaq 2454)"
"3832","(3832) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Amer bin Masoud Al-Qurashi, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If people knew what was in the first row, they would not have lined up in it except by drawing lots.\n(Bukhari 6151 Muslim 119)"
"3833","(3833) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, that Khaled bin Ma’dan He narrated to him, that Jubayr bin Nufir narrated to him, that Al-Irbad bin Sariyah narrated to him, and Al-Irbad was one of the companions of the Safa, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray three people in the front row, and one person in the second row.\n(Ahmad 4/1268 Ibn Hibban 6158)"
"3834","(3834) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: The best rows for men are the front, the worst are the back, and the best rows for women are the last. The worst of it is its introduction. (Ibn Majah 1001. Ahmad 3/387)"
"3835","(3835) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubair when The prayer has been established. He says: Come forward, come forward."
"3836","(3836) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Izar, on the authority of Abu Basir, he said: Ubayy ibn Ka’b said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The first row is perhaps like the row of angels, and if you knew, you would have rushed to it."
"3837","(3837) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he heard him say: The best ranks of men The front, the worst is the back, the best rows of women are the back, and the worst is the front."
"3838","(3838) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw him in the row. The one presenting Ruqqa said: Indeed, God and His angels are praying over the first rows, so the people crowded around him."
"3839","(3839) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: If you rise to... Prayer, so straighten your rows, and block the gap, for I see you behind my back."
"3840","(3840) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Sabit, who said: The feet did not change in Something more beloved to God than patches of row."
"3841","(3841) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: Ibn Umar saw a man praying with a clearing in front of him. In the classroom, he pushed him towards her."
"3842","(3842) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythama, who said: I prayed next to Ibn Umar, and he saw a relief in the row. So he motioned to me, but I did not move forward. He said: Then he moved forward and spoiled it."
"3843","(3843) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of And the relief, meaning in the classroom."
"3844","3844) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Maqbari, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever closes his gap in a row, God will raise him a rank therein, or build for him a house in Paradise."
"3845","(3845) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: It was said that."
"3846","(3846) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: For my doubles to fall is more beloved to me than If I see a defect in the class, I will not correct it."
"3847","(3847) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs, on the authority of his father, who said: We went out with Ibn Umar. He said: We prayed. The obligatory prayer, and he saw some of his children volunteering, so Ibn Omar said: I prayed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he refused. Bakr, Omar, and Othman, so there is no prayer before them or after them while traveling, and if you had volunteered, you would have completed it. (Bukhari 1102, Muslim 479)"
"3848","(3848) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: We asked him: Did Ibn Umar volunteer when travelling? He said: No, so I said: Two rak'ahs before dawn? He said: I did not see him leave your fig while traveling or at home."
"3849","(3849) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not perform voluntary prayers before or after the prayer while traveling, and he used to pray at night."
"3850","(3850) Hushaym told us, he said: Humayd, the client of the Ansar, told us, he said: I heard Abu Ja’far Muhammad bin Ali speaking, On the authority of his father Ali bin Hussein; He did not perform voluntary prayers while traveling before or after prayer."
"3851","(3851) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaman, who said: I saw a person volunteering to travel."
"3852","(3852) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; That his father used to travel voluntarily, and that Abdullah used to travel voluntarily."
"3853","(3853) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to volunteer while travelling."
"3854","(3854) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of a man called: Muhammad bin Qays, who said: I entered upon Jabir. Ibn Abdullah while he was voluntarily traveling."
"3855","(3855) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; Ali did not see any harm in voluntarily traveling."
"3856","(3856) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim; Ali volunteered to travel."
"3857","(3857) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; The Mother of the Believers used to travel voluntarily."
"3858","(3858) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; They did not see any harm in voluntarily traveling before or after prayer."
"3859","(3859) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I saw Al-Qasim volunteering to travel."
"3860","(3860) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi volunteering on a journey."
"3861","(3861) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Abu Dharr and Omar used to travel voluntarily."
"3862","(3862) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Abdullah’s companions used to volunteer when travelling."
"3863","(3863) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: My father used to pray after what was written in Traveling"
"3864","(3864) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: We agreed with the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they used to pray before and after the obligatory prayer, meaning when travelling."
"3865","(3865) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I accompanied Ibn Umar from Medina to Mecca, and it was He performs the voluntary prayer on his animal wherever it is mounted. If it is the obligatory prayer, he descends and prays."
"3866","(3866) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ash’ath, who said: I accompanied my father, Al-Aswad bin Yazid, and Amr bin Maymun. And Abu Wael, they used to pray two rak'ahs, then they would pray two rak'ahs after that."
"3867","(3867) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, Ash’ath, and Hajjaj, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace; He used to volunteer while travelling."
"3868","(3868) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salem; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Omar used to travel voluntarily."
"3869","(3869) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the traveler enters the prayer of those staying, he prays With their prayers"
"3870","(3870) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He prays with their prayers."
"3871","(3871) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning a traveler who performed a rak'ah from the prayer of residents, he said: He will pray with them and perform what he had previously done."
"3872","(3872) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If the traveler enters The prayer of the residents, pray with their prayers."
"3873","(3873) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He stayed for two years, praying two rak’ahs, except To pray with a people and perform their prayers."
"3874","(3874) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan. They said: He prays with their prayers."
"3875","(3875) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul; The traveler performs one or two rak'ahs from the resident's prayer; Let him pray with their prayers."
"3876","(3876) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, who said: I came to Medina and performed a rak’ah of dinner, so I performed I tell myself how to do? So I mentioned that to Al-Qasim, and he said: Were you afraid that if you prayed four times, God would punish you?"
"3877","(3877) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you catch up with the prayer of the residents, perform a rak’ah So perform their prayers."
"3878","(3878) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Concerning the traveler in the prayer of the residents, he said: He prays with their prayer."
"3879","(3879) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Mukhtar bin Amr Al-Azdi told us, he said: I asked Jabir bin Zaid about prayer while travelling? He said: So he said: If you pray alone, pray two rak’ahs, and if you pray in congregation, perform their prayer."
"3880","(3880) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Imran ibn Husayn, who said: I stayed with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the conquest of Mecca, stayed for eighteen nights, praying only two rak’ahs, then He says to the people of the town: Pray four times, for we are a traveling people. (Tirmidhi 545, Abu Dawud 1222)"
"3881","(3881) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar (h) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar (h) and on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar; He prayed two rak'ahs in Mecca, then he said: We are a traveling people, so complete the prayer."
"3882","(3882) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, with something similar."
"3883","(3883) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Omar, with something similar."
"3884","(3884) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I prayed two rak’ahs with Omar. In Mecca, then he said: O people of Mecca, we are a people on a journey, so complete the prayer."
"3885","(3885) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Omar (H) and on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, On the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, like him."
"3886","(3886) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray for his camel. (Bukhari 430, Abu Dawud 692)"
"3887","(3887) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ziyad al-Musaffar, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of al-Miqdam Al-Rawi, he said: Ubadah bin Al-Samit, Abu Al-Darda’, and Al-Harith bin Muawiyah sat down, and Abu Al-Darda’ said: Which of you? He mentions the hadith of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he prayed to a camel of spoils, and his servants said: I do. He said: So he narrated, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over a camel of spoils. (Ibn Majah 2850)"
"3888","(3888) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Salam, who said: Abu Idris Al-Khawlani narrated to us; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on the back of a camel."
"3889","(3889) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Ibn Umar used to pray to the camel when it was mounted."
"3890","(3890) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to display his camel and pray to it."
"3891","(3891) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw a man praying, and between him and the qiblah was a camel on top of him. Loaded"
"3892","(3892) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Ala, who said: I saw Suwayd ibn Ghafali Yunukh. His mount is on the way to Mecca, and he prays there."
"3893","(3893) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Al-Aswad; He was praying to his mount, and there was a clearing in front of him."
"3894","(3894) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim praying to... With their camels"
"3895","(3895) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He covers himself with a camel."
"3896","(3896) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him covering himself with a camel."
"3897","(3897) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal Al-Muzani, he said: The Prophet said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Pray in sheep’s pens, and do not pray in camels’ stalls, for they were created from the devils.\n(Ibn Majah 769 and Ibn Hibban 1702)"
"3898","(3898) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin He is single. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about praying in a camel shed? He said: Do not pray in it, and he was asked about praying in sheep pens? He said: Pray over it, for it is a blessing."
"3899","(3899) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and something like it, but he did not mention it: for it is a blessing."
"3900","(3900) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If you find nothing but sheep pens and camel pens, then pray in sheep pens, and do not pray in pens. Camels (Tirmidhi 348 and Ibn Hibban 1384)"
"3901","(3901) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin Al-Rabi’ bin Sabrah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He should not pray in camels’ stalls, but should pray in sheep’s cribs.\n(Ahmad 3/102. Daraqutni 276)"
"3902","(3902) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Abi Thawr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: He prays In sheep pens, and one should not pray in camels’ stalls."
"3903","(3903) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Ma’iz bin Nadli, he said: Abu Dharr came to us, entered a flock of our sheep, and prayed in it."
"3904","(3904) Abd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: A man narrated to me who asked Abd Allah bin Omar about the prayer in Ataan. Camels? He said: So he forbade it, and said: Pray in the sheep’s resting places."
"3905","(3905) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He prayed in the sheep pens before the mosque was built. (Bukhari 429. Muslim 374)"
"3906","(3906) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul Rahman; Omar prayed in a place where there was mud."
"3907","(3907) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sakhr bin Juwayriyah, on the authority of Asim bin al-Mundhir, who said: Ibn Al-Zubair went to Muzdalifah in other than the months of Hajj, so he led us in prayer in the sheep’s pastures, and he found another place, if only He wished to pray over them, and I did not see him doing that except to show us."
"3908","(3908) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: I heard Muhammad saying: Whenever they found nothing, they They pray in sheep pens and camel pens. They pray in sheep pens."
"3909","(3909) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abraham, who said: Pray in the fat of sheep."
"3910","(3910) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to pray on camels’ sheep’s milk, and he did not see any harm in it on sheep’s sheep’s milk."
"3911","(3911) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Hamza, who said: I heard Ubaid bin Umair say: Indeed, I have a hug that sleeps. Come with me in my mosque, and you will wander in it."
"3912","(3912) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jundub bin Amir Al-Salami; He used to pray in camel pens and sheep pens."
"3913","(3913) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of someone who heard Jabir ibn Samurah say: We were We pray in sheep pens, but we do not pray in camel pens."
"3914","(3914) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, he said: a man told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: Pray In sheep pens, and do not pray in camels’ stalls."
"3915","(3915) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: There is no harm in praying in sheep’s land."
"3916","(3916) Waki’ told us; Concerning a man who prayed with camel meat, that is sufficient, but he does not perform ablution from camel meat."
"3917","(3917) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Abi Thawr, on the authority of Jabir bin Samarra said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to pray in sheep pens, and not to pray in barns. Camels"
"3918","(3918) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a drop of urine that got on a sock? One of them said: He will celebrate, and the other said: He will not celebrate."
"3919","(3919) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; A number of them mentioned Abu Jafar; Because they did not repeat the prayer because of the sprinkling of urine and blood."
"3920","(3920) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man prays, he finds that after he had prayed, his garment was If he found drops or urine on his skin, he washed it and repeated the prayer, and if he found semen or blood on his skin, he washed it and did not repeat the prayer. Prayer"
"3921","(3921) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far al-Razi, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: Smiling In prayer, there is nothing."
"3922","(3922) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Smiling does not stop, but it does. The gurgling"
"3923","(3923) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Smiling during prayer is nothing."
"3924","(3924) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Smiling during prayer is not even a thing. He gurgles."
"3925","(3925) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They did not see anything in smiling during prayer."
"3926","(3926) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam Ibn Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He was asked about smiling during prayer? So he recited these verses: {Then he smiled, laughing at her words} I do not know how to smile except as laughter."
"3927","(3927) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Whenever Al-Hasan ibn Muslim saw me, he would smile at me. His face, while he was praying."
"3928","(3928) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: There is no harm in smiling."
"3929","(3929) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If a man laughs during prayer, he repeats it. Prayer and no longer performing ablution."
"3930","(3930) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, he said: I laughed behind My father, while I was praying, he ordered me to repeat the prayer."
"3931","(3931) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, he said: I laughed while I I was praying with my father, so he ordered me to repeat the prayer."
"3932","(3932) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He repeats the prayer, but he does not repeat it. Ablution"
"3933","(3933) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, who said: My brother laughed during prayer, so Urwah told him to stop. To repeat the prayer, and he did not command him to repeat the ablution."
"3934","(3934) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; About a man laughing during prayer, and he said: If he smiles then he should not leave, and if he laughs then he begins the prayer, and he does not have to perform ablution."
"3935","(3935) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: They were on a journey. So Abu Musa led them in prayer, then a one-eyed man fell into a well, or something, and all the people laughed, except for Abu Musa and Al-Ahnaf. So he ordered them to repeat the prayer."
"3936","(3936) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to command us when we were children. We laughed during the prayer so that we would repeat the prayer."
"3937","(3937) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; About a man laughing during prayer. He said: He says “Allahu Akbar” and repeats the prayer."
"3938","(3938) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He was leading his companions in prayer, when a blind man came and fell into a well in the mosque. Some of his companions laughed at him, so when he left He commanded whoever laughed to repeat the ablution and prayer. (Daraqutni 42. Abd al-Razzaq 3763)"
"3939","(3939) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amer, who said: This is a temptation, the Eid of ablution and prayer."
"3940","(3940) Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man laughs during prayer, he repeats the ablution. And the prayer\nAbu Bakr said: He repeats the prayer, but does not repeat the ablution."
"3941","(3941) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was desirable for one who prayed while sitting. To pray two rak'ahs while standing."
"3942","(3942) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It was desirable for someone who prayed while sitting, to stand up while sitting. Standing"
"3943","(3943) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yassaf, who said: Perhaps I prayed while sitting, so if I wanted To kneel, I got up and recited, then I bowed."
"3944","(3944) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And he said the salaam and prayed the night prayer standing, and when he entered the age, he began to pray sitting, so there remained thirty or forty days of prayer for him. He stood up and recited it, then prostrated. (Bukhari 1148 and Abu Dawud 950)"
"3945","(3945) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He said the salaam and prayed while sitting. When thirty verses of the surah remained, or forty verses, he stood up, recited, then bowed. (Muslim 505)"
"3946","(3946) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Whoever recites while sitting, then he kneels and prostrates while he is He is sitting, and whoever recites while standing, he should bow and prostrate while standing. Al-Hasan said: He has the choice. He did whatever he wanted."
"3947","(3947) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm for a man to pray while standing, standing. And kneeling, sitting."
"3948","(3948) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Shu`abi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: There is no harm for a man to pray in Rak’ah, standing. And kneeling, sitting. Then he said: Waki` told us another story: on the authority of his people, on the authority of al-Hikam, and he did not mention Hammad."
"3949","(3949) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He did not pray two rak’ahs. Fajr while traveling."
"3950","(3950) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: As for what he left neither healthy nor sick in Traveling, not present, absent, not witnessing, meaning the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, so two rak’ahs before dawn."
"3951","(3951) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi say: They were not They should pray four rak'ahs before noon, and two rak'ahs before dawn in any case."
"3952","(3952) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Habib ibn Jariya, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not He omits the two rak'ahs after sunset, and the two rak'ahs before dawn when he is home, and does not travel."
"3953","(3953) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I asked him if Ibn Umar used to pray. The two rak'ahs of Fajr? He said: I have not seen him leave anything behind while traveling or at home."
"3954","(3954) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Saif Al-Ansi narrated to me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Ghutaif, or Ghudayf bin Al-Harith Al-Kindi, Muawiyah doubted, saying: Whatever I saw, I forgot. I have not forgotten that I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placing his right hand on his left, meaning in prayer.\n(Ahmad 4/1051 Tabarani 3399)"
"3955","(3955) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qubaisa bin Halab, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, placing his right hand on his left in prayer. (Tirmidhi 252. Ahmad 4/226)"
"3956","(3956) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Asim ibn Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Wa’il ibn Hajar, who said: I saw the Messenger of God When he grew up, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he took his left hand with his right hand. (Ibn Majah 810)"
"3957","(3957) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijali, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’ said: One of the morals of the Prophets is to place the right over the left in prayer. (Ibn Hibban 1770, Tabarani 11485)"
"3958","(3958) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Maymun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is as if I am looking at the rabbis of the Children of Israel, placing their oaths on their left hands during prayer."
"3959","(3959) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Umair, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Wa’il bin Hajar, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He placed his right hand on his left during prayer, under the navel."
"3960","(3960) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He places his right hand on his left. Prayer under the navel."
"3961","(3961) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Salam bin Shaddad al-Jariri Abu Talut narrated to us, on the authority of Ghazwan bin Jarir al-Dhabi, on the authority of My father, he said: When Ali stood for prayer, he would place his right hand on his wrist, and he would not remain like that until he bowed. Whenever he bows, he only fixes his clothes or rubs his body."
"3962","(3962) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi al-Ja`d narrated to us, on the authority of Asim al-Jahdari, on the authority of Uqba bin Dhahir, on the authority of Ali: In his saying {Pray to your Lord and sacrifice} he said: placing the right hand over the left in prayer."
"3963","(3963) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Hassan told us, he said: I heard Abu Majliz, or I asked him, he said I said: How should I do? He said: He places the inside of his right hand on the inside of his left hand, and makes it lower than the navel."
"3964","(3964) Yazid told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Abi Zainab told us, he said: Abu Uthman told me; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by a man who was praying and he had placed his left hand on his right, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, took May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he placed his right hand on his left."
"3965","(3965) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in placing the right hand on someone. The left side in prayer."
"3966","(3966) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Zayd al-Sawa’i, on the authority of Abu Juhayfa On the authority of Ali, he said: Among the Sunnah of prayer is placing the hands on the hands under the bed. (Abu Dawud 4950, Dar Qatni 286)"
"3967","(3967) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Ziyad, the client of the Darraj family, who said: What I saw and forgot, for I have not forgotten that when Abu Bakr stood up for prayer, he said: This is how he placed the right hand on me. Al-Yasriya."
"3968","(3968) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to place the right hand on the left, so he said on his palm, or on the wrist, and he said on top of that, And the People of the Book say, “They will do it.”"
"3969","(3969) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Mustamir ibn al-Rayyan, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza’i; He used to order his companions to place his right hand on his left hand and pray."
"3970","(3970) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h), and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; They used to raise their hands during prayer."
"3971","(3971) Affan told us, he said: Zaid bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I heard Amr bin Dinar, he said: Ibn al-Zubayr was May God send his hand."
"3972","(3972) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He was asked about a man who held his right hand to his left? He said: He only did that for the sake of bloodshed."
"3973","(3973) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, who said: I did not see Ibn Al-Musayyab holding his right hand in The prayer, he used to send it."
"3974","(3974) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Aizar, who said: I was walking around with Saeed bin Jubayr. He saw a man praying, placing one hand on the other, this one on the other, and the other on the other, so he went. So he separated them and then came."
"3975","(3975) Hushaym told us, he said: Khalid and Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar; Ibn Masoud prayed while there was dirt and blood on his stomach. He said: He did not repeat the prayer."
"3976","(3976) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He refrained from this hadith after that, but he did not like it."
"3977","(3977) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There are no pumpings of blood that would harm a man. His prayers"
"3978","(3978) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shaybā, on the authority of Qāriḥ his brother, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; He would not stop bleeding until it was equal to the size of a dirham."
"3979","(3979) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad? Al-Hakam said: If it is the size of a dirham, and Hammad said: If it is the size of a mithqal, then he said: Or a dirham."
"3980","(3980) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabi’, he said: I saw a mujahid with blood on his garment praying for days."
"3981","(3981) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Saleh, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who prayed with blood on his clothes, he said: He will not celebrate Eid."
"3982","(3982) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw Abu Wa’il praying, and on his garment were drops of Blood"
"3983","(3983) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yasin, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If the value of a dirham is equal, it will be returned."
"3984","(3984) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say that there would be as much blood on the garment as a dinar or dirham. He said: Let him count."
"3985","(3985) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about a man who saw blood on his clothes. And he is in prayer? He said: If it is a lot, then let him drop the garment, and if it is a little, then let him continue with his prayer."
"3986","(3986) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: I asked him about the blood he saw on my clothes after What should I pray? He said: Wash him and repeat the prayer."
"3987","(3987) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who prayed with blood on his clothes. When he left, he saw it and said: He will not celebrate the Eid."
"3988","(3988) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you prayed and you see blood on your garment, do not repeat it. Your prayer has passed."
"3989","(3989) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’; He did not think that the blood and semen in the garment would cause the prayer to be repeated from him."
"3990","(3990) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who prayed with blood on his clothes, he said: If it was a lot, he should repeat the prayer, and if it was a little, he should not repeat it."
"3991","(3991) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw him praying and there was a handful of blood on his garment."
"3992","(3992) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn al-Salt. Omar washed what he saw in his clothes, sprinkled what he did not see, and returned after the dawn prayer had risen, feeling strong."
"3993","(3993) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar; That Omar prayed his lunch prayer, then he went to a place of his own in Al-Jurf, and he found a wet dream in his clothes. He said: So he washed off the wet dream. He took a bath, then repeated his morning prayer."
"3994","(3994) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aflah, on the authority of his father, who said: I prayed while wearing my funeral garment, so Ibn Umar ordered me to So she prepared."
"3995","(3995) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man praying with a funeral garment on him. He said: His prayer has ended, and there is no need to repeat it."
"3996","(3996) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus and Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: He will repeat what was at a certain time."
"3997","(3997) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab; He said: Whoever prays with ritual impurity on his garment, there is no need to repeat it."
"3998","(3998) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he found blood or semen on his garment, he washed it, and did not He counts the prayer."
"3999","(3999) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazeed, he said: Abdullah was He rises in prayer on the tops of his feet."
"4000","(4000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yazid, on the authority of Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Jaad said: Ali used to stand on the tops of his feet during prayer."
"4001","(4001) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Zayd, he said: It was Abdullah He rises in prayer on the tops of his feet."
"4002","(4002) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I saw him getting up for prayer. On the tops of his feet."
"4003","(4003) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, who said: Ibn Abi Layla used to get up for prayer. On the tops of his feet."
"4004","(4004) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Issa bin Misra, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Omar, Ali, and the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stand on the tops of their feet in prayer."
"4005","(4005) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Wahhab bin Kaysan, who said: I saw Ibn When Zubair prostrated the second prostration, he stood as he was on the tops of his feet."
"4006","(4006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr; In the same way"
"4007","(4007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Asama, and Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to stand on the tops of his feet during prayer."
"4008","(4008) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abu al-Mu’alla, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Ibn Masoud was in the rak’ah. The first and third: He does not sit when he wants to stand until he stands up."
